1
00:00:03,150 --> 00:02:03,150
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

2
00:02:04,185 --> 00:02:08,264
No living being was harmed during
the filming of this series.

3
00:02:09,185 --> 00:02:11,755
Episode 120

4
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:17,510
Your soul and blood are mine, Osman.

5
00:02:18,885 --> 00:02:20,715
You will die.

6
00:02:20,915 --> 00:02:23,485
Dying is hard, but killing is easy.

7
00:02:23,515 --> 00:02:24,815
Come and see.

8
00:02:24,855 --> 00:02:26,195
Come here.

9
00:02:28,985 --> 00:02:30,345
Wait.

10
00:02:32,685 --> 00:02:34,005
Wait.

11
00:02:46,495 --> 00:02:49,075
Wait.

12
00:02:55,445 --> 00:02:57,025
Wait.

13
00:03:03,625 --> 00:03:04,515
Now!

14
00:03:04,535 --> 00:03:07,075
O Allah!

15
00:03:07,185 --> 00:03:09,525
Attack!

16
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:01,370
You, Nayman!

17
00:04:09,650 --> 00:04:14,900
With this wounded hand, you can't
even graze a sheep, son of Osman.

18
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,450
Will you kill me with it?

19
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:19,759
Attack me while you have the chance.

20
00:04:19,769 --> 00:04:21,860
You may not have
the chance anymore.

21
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:33,550
You are brave, but courage is not enough.

22
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:44,040
You are weak, Orhan.

23
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:46,600
I am strong as I can
take your breath away.

24
00:04:54,350 --> 00:04:57,660
Your strength is not
enough to defeat me.

25
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:02,140
But I am the one
who can give you strength.

26
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:04,140
I don't want anything from you.

27
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,540
The only thing I will take
from you is your life.

28
00:05:06,570 --> 00:05:08,470
My hands will heal in time.

29
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:13,890
Nayman is greater than time.

30
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:09,900
Fire Turkish arrows at
the chests of the infidels!

31
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:12,890
Mashallah!

32
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:39,630
If you want to find medicine,
you must come to my camp.

33
00:07:58,310 --> 00:08:01,480
What is happening?
Who is this man?

34
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:11,750
Come on, they are
waiting for you at the palace.

35
00:08:12,510 --> 00:08:15,070
You go brother, I have some work
to do.

36
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:18,170
Be careful, brother, don't be late.

37
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:26,130
I'll come in time, you go.

38
00:09:23,770 --> 00:09:26,340
We fall to the ground for our calling...

39
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:27,880
...but you...

40
00:09:28,030 --> 00:09:30,170
Your death is in vain.

41
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,840
Come here.

42
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:33,460
Come here

43
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,510
Come here.

44
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,370
Come here.

45
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,060
Sit here.

46
00:09:44,490 --> 00:09:48,500
Nayman will send you
to the bottom of the earth!

47
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:50,950
And Nayman will come to you soon.

48
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:55,330
Then you ask him if he killed me or not.

49
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:02,600
Come here, get up.

50
00:10:08,590 --> 00:10:11,100
We will all die.

51
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:16,220
However, Erlik Khan...

52
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:18,350
We will all die.

53
00:10:18,970 --> 00:10:20,300
All of us.

54
00:10:21,110 --> 00:10:26,960
But our only wish is that
the dust we fall upon becomes our home.

55
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:31,740
May it be a home for us
to make it a shield for the oppressed.

56
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:39,930
But we will not allow
people like you to breathe.

57
00:10:40,710 --> 00:10:42,860
It's time.

58
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:16,900
Allah is the greatest!

59
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,040
O Allah.

60
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:21,700
Öktem tribe

61
00:11:23,665 --> 00:11:26,735
What's on your mind, mother?

62
00:11:27,795 --> 00:11:30,185
It hasn't been forty
days since my father's death.

63
00:11:30,255 --> 00:11:33,055
Why are you asking for
a wedding so quickly?

64
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:46,430
Your father's absence burns my soul too.

65
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:52,100
The deceased was not just your father.

66
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:57,660
Rather, he was my husband, the Bey
of my tribe, and the pillar of my tent.

67
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:59,770
My heart aches too.

68
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:02,250
Does your heart ache like this way?

69
00:12:02,270 --> 00:12:04,160
Speaking of the wedding?

70
00:12:05,010 --> 00:12:07,550
You said what you
said, so let me say it too.

71
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:11,340
The wedding will not take
place until my mourning is over.

72
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:18,960
Do I care about the wedding
or feast, Alçiçek?

73
00:12:20,930 --> 00:12:24,470
But the marriage will happen.

74
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:26,910
It needs to be done.

75
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:31,370
Don't you still
understand why I do this?

76
00:12:33,130 --> 00:12:35,870
Look at this chair well

77
00:12:38,010 --> 00:12:44,580
Beys are silent now that I sit on it.

78
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:50,160
But when our pain subsides, they
will strongly object to that.

79
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:54,270
You...

80
00:12:54,390 --> 00:12:59,420
I'll make Aktemur sit on the chair before
Beys object to my sitting on it.

81
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:03,470
Aktemur?

82
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,580
But he will not accept.

83
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:07,330
He's the Subasi in Yenişehir.

84
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:09,790
He will accept, we have
no other solution.

85
00:13:10,470 --> 00:13:15,930
If Aktemur doesn't sit on the it, forget
about the Kargın tribe, my daughter.

86
00:13:16,550 --> 00:13:19,860
If I knew Aktemur even a little bit,
he wouldn't accept it.

87
00:13:19,890 --> 00:13:21,250
He will.

88
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:24,060
Are you the woman he loves?

89
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:26,870
You will convince him.

90
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:28,790
How am I going to do this?

91
00:13:30,060 --> 00:13:34,180
Alçiçek, use your brain, daughter.

92
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:40,260
You can make him do
anything you ask him to do.

93
00:13:41,390 --> 00:13:45,560
But know that this is not for me.

94
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:47,700
And not for yourself.

95
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:52,270
Rather, you will do it to preserve our
tribe, your father's trust in us.

96
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:59,820
Go talk to Aktemur now.

97
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:05,350
Yenişehir

98
00:14:05,705 --> 00:14:09,255
Bengi Hatun wants to make
Aktemur the Bey of her tribe.

99
00:14:12,775 --> 00:14:14,835
What do you say, Bala?

100
00:14:14,955 --> 00:14:16,835
Who said this?

101
00:14:17,815 --> 00:14:20,405
No one needs to say anything

102
00:14:20,955 --> 00:14:24,095
Why do you think Bengi wants
the marriage quickly?

103
00:14:26,275 --> 00:14:29,765
Doesn't she sit on the
seat of sovereignty?

104
00:14:30,825 --> 00:14:34,305
Why does she want to make Aktemur
Bey sit on it? I don't understand.

105
00:14:35,715 --> 00:14:38,515
Also, there is a period of
mourning for her husband.

106
00:14:39,235 --> 00:14:40,975
What makes sense to do such a thing?

107
00:14:44,115 --> 00:14:45,705
Bengi.

108
00:14:47,155 --> 00:14:49,145
She is well-calculated.

109
00:14:49,255 --> 00:14:53,855
She knows very well that the Beys will
revolt when the mourning is over.

110
00:14:54,055 --> 00:14:55,075
Yes.

111
00:14:55,105 --> 00:14:58,985
She wants to get Aktemur to
sit before the Beys revolt.

112
00:15:04,325 --> 00:15:08,375
She will make Aktemur a Beys
and use it as she pleases.

113
00:15:08,415 --> 00:15:09,595
No.

114
00:15:09,685 --> 00:15:11,985
Aktemur will never allow this.

115
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:13,585
No!

116
00:15:17,455 --> 00:15:19,475
Aktemur is a smart man.

117
00:15:19,545 --> 00:15:22,985
And he knows he shouldn't do
anything without Osman Bey's permission.

118
00:15:24,695 --> 00:15:26,375
However...

119
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:31,015
Aktemur is also a kind person.

120
00:15:31,865 --> 00:15:35,345
May his mercy not drag
him into wrongdoing.

121
00:15:36,055 --> 00:15:40,155
I'm not going to let her take
advantage of my son, Malhun.

122
00:15:40,825 --> 00:15:45,615
She can't make Atktemur sit on the seat of
sovereignty and use him as she pleases.

123
00:15:46,075 --> 00:15:47,655
I will not allow her.

124
00:15:48,035 --> 00:15:50,435
Alçiçek won't allow this.

125
00:15:51,475 --> 00:15:54,595
Let's pray she won't be
complacent with this.

126
00:15:56,895 --> 00:16:00,615
What's more important than the words
and approval of others...

127
00:16:01,355 --> 00:16:05,985
is what Osman Bey will say
when we tell him

128
00:16:26,805 --> 00:16:28,365
- Boran.
- My Bey.

129
00:16:28,515 --> 00:16:30,855
Send half of the Alps to Yenişehir...

130
00:16:30,925 --> 00:16:32,795
and increase the measures.

131
00:16:33,155 --> 00:16:35,625
Obviously, Nayman wouldn't sit still.

132
00:16:35,695 --> 00:16:37,315
Your command, my Bey.

133
00:16:37,395 --> 00:16:39,035
- Turgut Bey.
- Yes, Osman Bey.

134
00:16:39,095 --> 00:16:41,905
Send Alps to and around İnegöl.

135
00:16:43,475 --> 00:16:46,755
Nayman will think we died here.

136
00:16:48,495 --> 00:16:53,295
He will try to attack
our property.

137
00:16:53,855 --> 00:16:57,935
Alps never lose sight in İnegöl.

138
00:16:58,235 --> 00:17:00,515
Don't worry.

139
00:17:04,505 --> 00:17:06,365
What should we do now, my Bey?

140
00:17:07,125 --> 00:17:08,973
We will go to Söğüt.

141
00:17:14,223 --> 00:17:15,575
My Bey.

142
00:17:17,085 --> 00:17:19,415
What are we going to do
with these soldiers?

143
00:17:26,155 --> 00:17:28,044
Take them and put
them in the cart.

144
00:17:28,125 --> 00:17:30,585
Put them in the cart and
send them to their owner.

145
00:17:32,775 --> 00:17:35,215
And fill their mouths with dirt.

146
00:17:35,455 --> 00:17:40,575
Fill it in to see the fate of
those who covet our lands.

147
00:17:41,225 --> 00:17:42,605
Come on.

148
00:17:42,685 --> 00:17:44,225
Your command, my Bey.

149
00:17:54,750 --> 00:17:56,330
Drom where is this?

150
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:59,410
I do not want a foreign work, but
rather a Turkish work.

151
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:01,210
We don't have any foreign work.

152
00:18:01,290 --> 00:18:04,580
It is a Turkish work made
by the neighboring tribes.

153
00:18:05,870 --> 00:18:07,630
No, not this.

154
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:09,400
I want the best.

155
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:11,630
I am preparing a dowry for my daughter.

156
00:18:11,870 --> 00:18:14,240
Well, take your pick and prepare.

157
00:18:14,290 --> 00:18:17,040
Send these to the palace of Osman Bey.

158
00:18:19,430 --> 00:18:21,170
Osman Bey's palace?

159
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:22,660
Yes.

160
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:24,460
Who are you, Hatun?

161
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:26,410
That's none of your business.

162
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:27,760
Do your job.

163
00:18:29,310 --> 00:18:31,990
They say curiosity kills a man,
don't you know that?

164
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,510
Excuse me, I was surprised when
you said "Osman Bey's palace."

165
00:18:48,750 --> 00:18:50,990
What am I going to do now, Kumral Abdal?

166
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:53,970
How am I going to make
things up with Ülgen Hatun?

167
00:18:57,160 --> 00:19:00,130
Your treatment is there.

168
00:19:05,330 --> 00:19:07,550
Come on, get your money bag out.

169
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:08,840
Come on.

170
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:11,960
What do I do with the bag?
Shall I give her money?

171
00:19:12,390 --> 00:19:15,690
Of course, you will not go empty-handed
to ask for her forgiveness.

172
00:19:15,810 --> 00:19:17,090
Shop.

173
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:18,920
Come on, to the shop.

174
00:19:18,990 --> 00:19:21,620
Thank you, Kumral Abdal!

175
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:23,940
Look at me.

176
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:25,340
Yes?

177
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:27,730
Do you have another color?

178
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:30,800
Here, on this side, there
is also the color red.

179
00:19:44,930 --> 00:19:47,020
Give it to me, young man.

180
00:19:52,290 --> 00:19:55,060
I caught it
first, don't take offense.

181
00:19:55,090 --> 00:19:57,430
It's mine and you
should pick from other fabrics.

182
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:59,210
I need a red cloth.

183
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:01,460
Leave it!

184
00:20:01,490 --> 00:20:03,200
Oh my!

185
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:05,300
I told you I caught it first, grandmother.

186
00:20:05,330 --> 00:20:08,210
This cloth is mine, don't be
stubborn, it's important!

187
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:11,560
Cerkutay!

188
00:20:12,510 --> 00:20:15,020
Leave it, choose another fabric.

189
00:20:15,770 --> 00:20:18,070
What you are doing is
disgraceful to the Hatun.

190
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:20,610
Is that a disgrace to her
and not a disgrace to me?

191
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:22,240
I said I had it first!

192
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:24,240
Leave it!

193
00:20:24,270 --> 00:20:25,470
You leave it!

194
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:28,270
Leave him, you damned!

195
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:30,240
Leave it! I hope your head cracks!

196
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:33,060
I will not leave it, if you leave it, you will fall.

197
00:20:33,130 --> 00:20:35,650
Also, I need this cloth.

198
00:20:35,750 --> 00:20:37,120
Leave it, I took it.

199
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,810
You lunatic!

200
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:43,630
I will spill your blood!

201
00:20:47,570 --> 00:20:49,150
Cerkutay.

202
00:21:03,650 --> 00:21:05,440
It can't be, Alçiçek.

203
00:21:05,710 --> 00:21:07,600
I am the Subasi of Yenişehir.

204
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:09,670
I do not covet sovereignty.

205
00:21:10,430 --> 00:21:13,280
Also, isn't there any man in this
large tribe to be the Bey?

206
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,980
Do I have a brother to hide
from you, Aktemur?

207
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:18,230
I don't have, don't you know?

208
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:20,190
Only my mother and I are here.

209
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:22,260
And we have no one else.

210
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:25,990
We don't.

211
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:30,690
We are alone.

212
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:35,410
You know I didn't mean to say that.

213
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,520
I am always by your side.

214
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:41,330
But I do not follow sovereignty.

215
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:43,420
This is not an issue of sovereignty.

216
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:45,480
Rather, it is an emergency.

217
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:48,590
Our tribe is my father's trust in us.

218
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:51,480
Will you not keep this trust?

219
00:21:55,170 --> 00:21:56,520
Also...

220
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:59,740
Beys of the tribe will not accept this.

221
00:21:59,810 --> 00:22:02,960
If you accept, the rest
doesn't matter to anyone.

222
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:06,480
My mother will speak to the Beys.

223
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:10,610
We don't have anyone as
good as you to be a Bey.

224
00:22:10,650 --> 00:22:16,160
There is no place in our tribe for a Bey who doesn't pledge allegiance to the son of Gündüz Bey.

225
00:22:18,850 --> 00:22:20,900
Do you think you can't do that?

226
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,430
Or are you afraid?

227
00:22:23,510 --> 00:22:25,330
What am I afraid of, Alçiçek?

228
00:22:25,710 --> 00:22:27,280
I am not afraid.

229
00:22:28,610 --> 00:22:30,500
However, Osman Bey...

230
00:22:33,250 --> 00:22:35,060
What does my uncle think about this?

231
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:38,160
I cannot do this
without consulting him.

232
00:22:38,180 --> 00:22:41,090
But you're in a hurry.

233
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:46,170
You're leaving me stuck
between you two, Alçiçek.

234
00:22:46,290 --> 00:22:49,020
Osman Bey left the
great Yenişehir as a trust to you.

235
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:52,750
Why would he be against you being
the Bey of the Kargın tribe?

236
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:55,950
The Kargın tribe is also related to the Kayı.

237
00:22:56,910 --> 00:23:00,330
But if you do not accept this trust...

238
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:03,760
my tribe will perish
and disappear, Aktemur.

239
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:07,350
I never liked this, Alçiçek.

240
00:23:07,390 --> 00:23:08,960
We have to.

241
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:11,560
We have to, Aktemur.

242
00:23:11,910 --> 00:23:13,980
My mother is sitting on the chair now.

243
00:23:14,150 --> 00:23:18,160
However, Beys will begin to disobey soon.

244
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:23,100
You're not going to sacrifice
your position in this mess, are you?

245
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:25,930
You're going to sit in the chair, right?

246
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:33,310
You hit me.

247
00:23:34,730 --> 00:23:36,270
You hit Cerkutay.

248
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:38,190
Whoa, whoa.

249
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:40,870
Who will take you from my hands now?

250
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:42,170
Come here!

251
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:43,960
Stop, Hatun, stop!

252
00:23:44,050 --> 00:23:45,810
Will you hit him with a sword?
Stop!

253
00:23:45,850 --> 00:23:47,750
Go away!

254
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:49,950
Give it to me!

255
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:54,190
Pray to Allah that you are not a man!

256
00:23:55,970 --> 00:23:59,190
I ignore this behavior of yours because
your old age, grandmother.

257
00:23:59,780 --> 00:24:00,870
Cerkutay.

258
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:02,430
Come over here!

259
00:24:02,590 --> 00:24:05,100
Stop, sister, stop, stop!

260
00:24:09,910 --> 00:24:11,410
You don't know.

261
00:24:12,140 --> 00:24:13,720
He's crazy.

262
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:16,640
What?
Are you telling the truth?

263
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:18,020
Yes.

264
00:24:23,710 --> 00:24:25,290
He's crazy.

265
00:24:26,420 --> 00:24:30,320
This is good, otherwise, I would
kill him.

266
00:24:31,050 --> 00:24:32,600
Okay then.

267
00:24:32,860 --> 00:24:35,380
You saved me from committing a great sin.

268
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:40,580
Otherwise, I wouldn't have cared that he was crazy
and would have knocked him to the ground!

269
00:24:43,890 --> 00:24:46,910
I think I know you...

270
00:24:54,270 --> 00:24:55,780
Kumral Abdal.

271
00:24:57,070 --> 00:24:58,890
This is you, right?

272
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:01,320
You...

273
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:04,040
You are...

274
00:25:08,460 --> 00:25:09,960
The brown midwife.

275
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:14,210
Feriştah Hatun?

276
00:26:15,985 --> 00:26:18,505
Where is Osman's head?

277
00:26:23,025 --> 00:26:24,545
Osman!

278
00:26:25,185 --> 00:26:28,355
He escaped the trap we
set, Commander Nayman.

279
00:26:35,155 --> 00:26:38,095
We didn't do it ourselves.

280
00:26:38,785 --> 00:26:42,605
He survived!

281
00:26:45,795 --> 00:26:47,625
Where is Gök Talay?

282
00:26:48,855 --> 00:26:50,955
Where is Gök Talay?

283
00:26:53,715 --> 00:26:55,435
Osman...

284
00:26:55,745 --> 00:26:58,205
Gök Talay's head...

285
00:27:13,435 --> 00:27:17,155
You weren't the only arrow I shot.

286
00:27:17,645 --> 00:27:19,725
Osman.

287
00:27:20,145 --> 00:27:22,955
He will come.

288
00:27:25,975 --> 00:27:28,815
Söğüt

289
00:27:31,785 --> 00:27:33,285
Celali.

290
00:27:33,455 --> 00:27:35,675
Are you the one who sold me?

291
00:27:38,465 --> 00:27:39,785
What are you saying?

292
00:27:40,395 --> 00:27:42,685
Bayındır...

293
00:27:43,165 --> 00:27:47,005
Since when does a dog do something without
its owner's knowledge, Mother Sultan?

294
00:27:47,185 --> 00:27:48,545
The dog remains a dog.

295
00:27:48,785 --> 00:27:51,445
His devotion is to himself only.

296
00:27:51,655 --> 00:27:56,215
We see his sincerity as long as we
benefit him, Osman Bey.

297
00:27:59,025 --> 00:28:03,075
Apparently, Nayman gave him more bone.

298
00:28:03,555 --> 00:28:06,845
However, I will kill Bayındır!

299
00:28:07,155 --> 00:28:09,005
Say, what did he give him?

300
00:28:14,315 --> 00:28:18,435
Mashallah!

301
00:28:27,755 --> 00:28:29,795
Slowly, slowly!

302
00:28:30,785 --> 00:28:32,805
These goods will go a long way.

303
00:28:33,335 --> 00:28:35,105
Move carefully.

304
00:28:48,925 --> 00:28:50,285
Hüseyin.

305
00:28:53,915 --> 00:28:56,445
I will be very rich, Hüseyin.

306
00:28:57,105 --> 00:29:00,395
After I set up Osman...

307
00:29:01,005 --> 00:29:04,485
there's no one
better than me for Nayman.

308
00:29:05,855 --> 00:29:08,745
It is true what you say.

309
00:29:08,955 --> 00:29:12,145
Genghis Khan's charter is
in my possession.

310
00:29:13,065 --> 00:29:15,635
Let's get out on the road..

311
00:29:18,255 --> 00:29:21,775
and take
these goods beyond the border areas.

312
00:29:23,755 --> 00:29:28,515
And then you will see that
everyone will kneel before me.

313
00:29:29,215 --> 00:29:34,745
There will be no ruling
left for İsmihan or Osman.

314
00:29:35,645 --> 00:29:37,945
I will not hear from any of them.

315
00:29:39,005 --> 00:29:40,895
Shall we go at once, my bey?

316
00:29:40,935 --> 00:29:42,765
Yes.

317
00:29:43,645 --> 00:29:48,235
It won't take long for İsmihan to find
out what we're weaving here.

318
00:29:48,295 --> 00:29:50,175
Well, what about Osman?

319
00:29:50,295 --> 00:29:52,165
If he escaped from the trap?

320
00:29:53,485 --> 00:29:55,325
What did we do, Hüseyin?

321
00:29:56,545 --> 00:29:58,865
We did our job.

322
00:30:00,785 --> 00:30:02,535
And we got our reward.

323
00:30:04,995 --> 00:30:09,325
I have to see Nayman before we go.

324
00:30:10,365 --> 00:30:11,615
Come on.

325
00:30:14,995 --> 00:30:16,755
I said what does he have?

326
00:30:16,955 --> 00:30:18,285
A charter.

327
00:30:18,785 --> 00:30:21,115
A charter that Genghis Khan
gave to merchants...

328
00:30:21,145 --> 00:30:25,555
so that they could move
between regions within his lands.

329
00:30:29,035 --> 00:30:32,125
This is not something
that can be given to anyone.

330
00:30:32,615 --> 00:30:36,065
You think of the value of your head, Osman Bey.

331
00:30:38,175 --> 00:30:39,995
But this is not important.

332
00:30:40,175 --> 00:30:43,875
I'll kill Bayındır as soon as possible.

333
00:30:44,075 --> 00:30:45,405
No.

334
00:30:46,775 --> 00:30:53,035
Bayındır will live a while.

335
00:30:53,845 --> 00:30:56,355
Will you pardon his betrayal, Osman Bey?

336
00:30:58,335 --> 00:31:02,475
You say that what he has enables him to
go from one area to another.

337
00:31:03,645 --> 00:31:06,005
We need the charter.

338
00:31:07,055 --> 00:31:09,155
And Bayındır.

339
00:31:09,725 --> 00:31:11,085
Why?

340
00:31:11,945 --> 00:31:13,695
To succeed first.

341
00:31:14,075 --> 00:31:18,125
Then, you will hear the reason with
everyone, Mother Sultan.

342
00:31:23,445 --> 00:31:26,505
She is not a woman but a beast.

343
00:31:26,675 --> 00:31:28,255
How did she hit my head?

344
00:31:28,665 --> 00:31:30,495
Her hand is very strong.

345
00:31:33,345 --> 00:31:34,435
What are you looking at?

346
00:31:34,975 --> 00:31:36,535
What are you looking at?

347
00:31:39,285 --> 00:31:41,145
Wise people can't find me!

348
00:31:42,805 --> 00:31:44,655
Cerkutay!

349
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:49,045
What did you do?

350
00:31:49,305 --> 00:31:53,235
It is nothing.

351
00:31:56,845 --> 00:32:00,395
It is nothing.

352
00:32:02,735 --> 00:32:06,825
I met a grandmother like
a monster in the market.

353
00:32:06,935 --> 00:32:08,215
And what?

354
00:32:08,255 --> 00:32:09,975
And...

355
00:32:10,825 --> 00:32:15,955
It seems that she knew that I made you
sad, so she spilled my blood.

356
00:32:16,555 --> 00:32:19,455
Yes, correct.

357
00:32:20,245 --> 00:32:21,965
She did a good job.

358
00:32:22,145 --> 00:32:23,525
Good.

359
00:32:23,825 --> 00:32:26,915
Stop it, Ülgen.

360
00:32:28,225 --> 00:32:29,735
Ülgen Hatun.

361
00:32:30,055 --> 00:32:32,145
A little time left for iftaar.

362
00:32:33,415 --> 00:32:35,605
I'll prepare the food, don't distract me.

363
00:32:35,875 --> 00:32:38,725
I don't distract you, I don't
distract you.

364
00:32:51,215 --> 00:32:52,875
Is this for me?

365
00:32:53,115 --> 00:32:54,395
Yes.

366
00:33:09,155 --> 00:33:10,835
Do you like it?

367
00:33:12,695 --> 00:33:16,185
It's very beautiful, I like it.

368
00:33:22,425 --> 00:33:28,485
But if you think I'll forgive you
for a piece of cloth, you're wrong...

369
00:33:29,185 --> 00:33:30,705
Cerkutay Alp.

370
00:33:31,125 --> 00:33:33,205
It is not an ordinary cloth.

371
00:33:33,765 --> 00:33:36,945
I argued with a monster for this cloth.

372
00:33:37,485 --> 00:33:39,325
I shed blood.

373
00:33:40,565 --> 00:33:41,885
Yes.

374
00:33:44,095 --> 00:33:46,855
That damned man!

375
00:33:49,635 --> 00:33:51,715
That wild woman hit my head so hard...

376
00:33:51,915 --> 00:33:54,265
that I can still hear her voice!

377
00:33:56,815 --> 00:33:58,335
Mother!

378
00:34:05,635 --> 00:34:07,155
Oh man!

379
00:34:07,975 --> 00:34:10,335
The brown midwife, Feriştah.

380
00:34:13,824 --> 00:34:15,405
Monster.

381
00:34:16,985 --> 00:34:20,085
- Is she your mother?
- Yes.

382
00:34:20,525 --> 00:34:22,755
Oh my.

383
00:34:23,425 --> 00:34:24,625
Ülgen!

384
00:34:24,965 --> 00:34:27,955
Why do you stand like a tree?
Come and take what's in my hand.

385
00:34:29,125 --> 00:34:30,485
Yes.

386
00:34:33,635 --> 00:34:35,145
Mother?

387
00:34:35,995 --> 00:34:36,955
Mother?

388
00:34:36,985 --> 00:34:38,315
My little girl!

389
00:34:39,103 --> 00:34:40,304
I missed you.

390
00:34:46,455 --> 00:34:48,185
Come on, mother.

391
00:35:03,235 --> 00:35:05,585
What is this lunatic doing here?

392
00:35:08,515 --> 00:35:10,085
- Lunatic?
- Lunatic?

393
00:35:20,265 --> 00:35:23,175
Yes, he's crazy.

394
00:35:23,205 --> 00:35:26,505
Mother, he's crazy walking around here.

395
00:35:27,395 --> 00:35:29,245
Come on, let's go inside.

396
00:35:32,625 --> 00:35:34,475
Come on, let's go inside.

397
00:35:43,285 --> 00:35:45,365
What does crazy mean?
What does crazy mean?

398
00:35:46,275 --> 00:35:48,075
I said that unintentionally.

399
00:35:59,425 --> 00:36:00,775
Cloth.

400
00:36:03,345 --> 00:36:05,365
The brown midwife Feriştah.

401
00:36:06,465 --> 00:36:08,275
You're done, Cerkutay.

402
00:36:10,075 --> 00:36:11,425
You're done.

403
00:36:13,065 --> 00:36:14,435
I'm done.

404
00:36:16,165 --> 00:36:17,505
I'm done.

405
00:36:21,450 --> 00:36:23,520
Yes, he is not in the palace either.

406
00:36:23,560 --> 00:36:25,400
So, where is this boy?

407
00:36:26,160 --> 00:36:27,660
Malhun.

408
00:36:28,580 --> 00:36:30,600
Aladdin is the last person to see Orhan.

409
00:36:31,420 --> 00:36:33,420
My brother was talking to a dervish.

410
00:36:34,110 --> 00:36:35,890
Who is that dervish?

411
00:36:37,180 --> 00:36:40,260
Then I said, let's go back
to the palace, and he said no.

412
00:36:41,670 --> 00:36:45,300
I reminded him of Kumral Abdal and
the importance of timing his medication.

413
00:36:45,460 --> 00:36:47,710
He said, "don't worry, I'll come in time."

414
00:36:48,670 --> 00:36:50,500
I was going to look at his hand.

415
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:53,440
I mean, I don't want to cause anxiety...

416
00:36:53,740 --> 00:36:56,240
he would come, Malhun Hatun.

417
00:36:56,670 --> 00:36:59,050
Who is that dervish, my son?
Didn't you see him?

418
00:36:59,710 --> 00:37:02,030
No, my brother spoke to him.

419
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:05,080
I asked him and he said he
was asking about the way.

420
00:37:05,100 --> 00:37:07,120
I wish I hadn't left him alone.

421
00:37:10,290 --> 00:37:12,690
Malhun, don't worry.

422
00:37:13,590 --> 00:37:15,340
The condition of his hand
disturbs him greatly.

423
00:37:15,370 --> 00:37:18,420
He clearly wants to practice on his own.

424
00:37:19,050 --> 00:37:20,760
You say so, however...

425
00:37:20,850 --> 00:37:24,280
even when he went to training,
he wouldn't go without my knowledge, Bala.

426
00:37:25,540 --> 00:37:28,410
I sent news to the warriors, we
will find him.

427
00:37:28,450 --> 00:37:29,980
Inshallah.

428
00:38:19,450 --> 00:38:21,210
Commander Nayman.

429
00:38:21,470 --> 00:38:22,980
Orhan is here.

430
00:38:46,660 --> 00:38:49,840
Welcome, son of Osman.

431
00:38:50,470 --> 00:38:53,060
I came to see if you were a man
of his word, Nayman.

432
00:38:54,980 --> 00:38:57,000
Can you treat my hand?

433
00:39:07,270 --> 00:39:10,360
Konur, take several warriors with you.

434
00:39:11,270 --> 00:39:15,540
When you meet with Turgut Bey
and his warriors, give him this.

435
00:39:17,230 --> 00:39:18,760
Your command, my Bey.

436
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:23,010
Bayındır is with Nayman.

437
00:39:23,540 --> 00:39:25,070
You will track him down.

438
00:39:25,510 --> 00:39:28,830
You will know every step he takes,
you will know all his campaigns.

439
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:35,230
My Bey, what is our purpose
in tracking him?

440
00:39:40,150 --> 00:39:43,730
Bayıdır is betraying us.

441
00:39:44,350 --> 00:39:49,530
As there is good in every evil, it
will benefit us.

442
00:39:50,890 --> 00:39:54,110
Come on, everyone back to work, we're
going to Yenişehir.

443
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:50,340
You will recover, son of Osman.

444
00:41:54,290 --> 00:41:56,330
We take good from all evil, Nayman.

445
00:41:57,900 --> 00:41:59,700
Be the reason for my recovery.

446
00:42:04,620 --> 00:42:07,750
May my healing be the reason
for our friendship.

447
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:30,810
No doubt, it will be done.

448
00:42:31,550 --> 00:42:33,110
Doubt is necessary.

449
00:42:34,460 --> 00:42:36,000
My body is healed.

450
00:42:37,620 --> 00:42:39,510
But what about my hands?

451
00:42:39,890 --> 00:42:41,900
So, you make me need you?

452
00:42:45,450 --> 00:42:47,300
So, I come here?

453
00:42:59,550 --> 00:43:00,860
Say it.

454
00:43:05,760 --> 00:43:10,320
You are brave, but you are fools.

455
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:15,100
Shall we carry him to the
tent, Commander Nayman?

456
00:43:15,490 --> 00:43:18,050
They consider themselves wolves...

457
00:43:18,910 --> 00:43:22,440
extreme cold heals wolves.
He will survive in extreme cold.

458
00:43:23,500 --> 00:43:24,800
He will heal.

459
00:43:56,720 --> 00:43:58,490
Commander Nayman.

460
00:43:59,230 --> 00:44:02,310
Bayındır and Vizier Saveli are here.

461
00:44:02,870 --> 00:44:04,260
Let them come.

462
00:44:35,230 --> 00:44:36,770
Commander Nayman.

463
00:44:38,030 --> 00:44:39,910
What is Orhan doing here?

464
00:44:40,440 --> 00:44:41,750
Don't you dare...

465
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:48,370
I heard that Osman is not dead and
that his son is sleeping here.

466
00:44:49,160 --> 00:44:51,660
Is your intention to make him kill me?

467
00:44:52,310 --> 00:44:55,680
Don't get caught up in
these things, merchant.

468
00:44:57,460 --> 00:45:04,650
You proved your loyalty by exposing
the game Osman set up for me.

469
00:45:05,490 --> 00:45:09,140
Your loyalty saves your soul.

470
00:45:10,830 --> 00:45:12,300
You passed the exam.

471
00:45:13,680 --> 00:45:15,450
You will be rewarded.

472
00:45:18,730 --> 00:45:22,880
You have given me the biggest reward.

473
00:45:24,890 --> 00:45:27,630
The gift of the great
Nayman cannot be returned.

474
00:45:37,640 --> 00:45:39,000
However...

475
00:45:41,450 --> 00:45:44,470
Don't check your stuff in vain, merchant.

476
00:45:48,270 --> 00:45:49,390
It's fake.

477
00:45:52,980 --> 00:45:55,060
It's not Genghis Khan's document.

478
00:45:55,450 --> 00:45:57,040
Not?

479
00:45:59,830 --> 00:46:01,420
No.

480
00:46:02,240 --> 00:46:05,310
If you took it out on the road...

481
00:46:07,550 --> 00:46:12,400
The first soldier to show it
would have cut your throat.

482
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:25,010
You will take this document.

483
00:46:26,360 --> 00:46:29,490
You'll give it to Talay and take the seal.

484
00:46:33,930 --> 00:46:35,280
Seal?

485
00:46:35,990 --> 00:46:37,680
Will the document not become
mine?

486
00:46:37,770 --> 00:46:44,800
All Mongols will unite under my shadow
when you bring that seal.

487
00:46:46,370 --> 00:46:48,210
No need for money.

488
00:46:48,660 --> 00:46:55,420
You'll get rich, anyway,
when I'm in charge.

489
00:46:59,820 --> 00:47:02,830
Yes, and what about Osman?

490
00:47:04,430 --> 00:47:06,150
If Osman is after the seal...

491
00:47:07,310 --> 00:47:12,630
your money will only keep the Mongol
soldiers out of my way, not Osman's.

492
00:47:19,390 --> 00:47:24,100
You will unite with my soldiers at
the position of Akçaağaç.

493
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:28,820
Then no one will stand in your way.

494
00:47:52,060 --> 00:47:54,110
Yenişehir

495
00:48:01,985 --> 00:48:03,485
Osman.

496
00:48:04,115 --> 00:48:05,375
Osman.

497
00:48:05,435 --> 00:48:07,255
What happened, Malhun?

498
00:48:07,735 --> 00:48:09,265
Is there bad news?

499
00:48:09,315 --> 00:48:12,085
Orhan is missing.
No one has seen my son.

500
00:48:12,405 --> 00:48:15,095
Where would he have gone in that state?
What is he doing?

501
00:48:15,505 --> 00:48:18,205
We sent warriors to the vicinity
of Yenişehir, but no one saw him.

502
00:48:18,225 --> 00:48:21,945
Aladdin is the last person to see him,
and he was talking to a dervish.

503
00:48:29,305 --> 00:48:31,195
You didn't find him anywhere, did you?

504
00:48:36,905 --> 00:48:38,945
Or do you know where he is?

505
00:48:48,135 --> 00:48:49,915
Orhan is on a mission.

506
00:48:50,085 --> 00:48:52,645
Alhamdulillah, we worried about him a lot

507
00:48:55,955 --> 00:48:58,935
If that's the case, why don't you tell us?

508
00:48:59,315 --> 00:49:02,405
Besides, what kind of mission
are you hiding even from us?

509
00:49:03,375 --> 00:49:04,725
Don't get upset.

510
00:49:05,405 --> 00:49:06,735
Don't be upset.

511
00:49:07,615 --> 00:49:09,425
I have also recently learned about it.

512
00:49:13,775 --> 00:49:15,755
My Bey, there is a knight coming.

513
00:49:27,775 --> 00:49:29,295
Orhan.

514
00:49:37,365 --> 00:49:38,935
Orhan.

515
00:49:40,215 --> 00:49:41,515
My Bey.

516
00:49:45,145 --> 00:49:46,715
Son, are you okay?

517
00:49:47,485 --> 00:49:50,535
Nayman met me today in Yenişehir.

518
00:49:54,295 --> 00:49:56,495
What are you saying?
Are you well?

519
00:49:57,385 --> 00:49:59,165
I'm fine, father.

520
00:50:00,445 --> 00:50:02,475
Nayman says he'll fix my hand.

521
00:50:03,515 --> 00:50:04,865
What?

522
00:50:13,595 --> 00:50:16,115
He says he will treat me if
I go to his camp.

523
00:50:18,005 --> 00:50:20,545
I want recovery more than anything else.

524
00:50:21,565 --> 00:50:23,355
But what I want most...

525
00:50:30,605 --> 00:50:32,305
What do you want?

526
00:50:34,805 --> 00:50:37,385
Son, say it.

527
00:50:38,555 --> 00:50:40,355
What do you want the most?

528
00:50:43,125 --> 00:50:44,985
If you are paralyzed or lame...

529
00:50:45,505 --> 00:50:48,185
those don't prevent us from
becoming a great country.

530
00:50:49,155 --> 00:50:52,015
But if I go to Nayman
and put you in a tough spot...

531
00:51:11,935 --> 00:51:14,495
May your heart always
beat with this calling.

532
00:51:16,005 --> 00:51:20,655
Then your body will heal and the
world will become our home too.

533
00:51:22,905 --> 00:51:24,265
Look.

534
00:51:25,745 --> 00:51:27,115
Son.

535
00:51:28,565 --> 00:51:30,135
It's your mission now.

536
00:51:32,765 --> 00:51:35,305
But you will open your
eyes and ears very well.

537
00:51:39,185 --> 00:51:41,075
May your conquest be blessed.

538
00:51:41,365 --> 00:51:43,255
May you be blessed,my Bey.

539
00:52:12,265 --> 00:52:14,015
He's going to Nayman.

540
00:52:18,135 --> 00:52:20,215
Nayman will fix his arm.

541
00:52:21,375 --> 00:52:23,245
What are you saying, Osman?

542
00:52:23,535 --> 00:52:26,675
We couldn't know what that dog would do.
How could you allow something like that?

543
00:52:26,795 --> 00:52:28,075
Malhun is right.

544
00:52:28,175 --> 00:52:30,175
- What if he did something to Orhan?
- No.

545
00:52:31,065 --> 00:52:33,095
Nayman can't do anything to him.

546
00:52:41,285 --> 00:52:43,045
What are you going to do with Orhan?

547
00:52:43,105 --> 00:52:46,125
Since he's here, you must have a plan.

548
00:52:46,445 --> 00:52:49,185
Let's kill him and finish
him off, Commander Nayman.

549
00:52:49,545 --> 00:52:51,755
What can this boy do for us?

550
00:52:51,855 --> 00:52:53,155
No.

551
00:52:54,505 --> 00:52:58,305
This will be the last example of my mercy.

552
00:52:58,825 --> 00:53:00,205
He will live.

553
00:53:01,165 --> 00:53:02,545
He will receive treatment.

554
00:53:06,045 --> 00:53:09,265
A hungry dog ​​bites its owner.

555
00:53:10,025 --> 00:53:13,195
First, you will fill your belly...

556
00:53:13,355 --> 00:53:14,655
and later...

557
00:53:15,005 --> 00:53:18,535
I will explain your task to you
step by step.

558
00:53:19,085 --> 00:53:20,405
Come on.

559
00:53:20,445 --> 00:53:21,815
Enter the tent.

560
00:53:21,835 --> 00:53:24,355
Thank you, Commander Natman, but...

561
00:53:25,245 --> 00:53:27,295
I am fasting.

562
00:53:30,815 --> 00:53:36,865
You know your gold won't
save you in the afterlife.

563
00:53:39,485 --> 00:53:42,055
Come in, Bayındır.

564
00:54:17,185 --> 00:54:19,705
We have surrounded the
headquarters from all sides.

565
00:54:21,935 --> 00:54:23,785
As Osman Bey said...

566
00:54:24,145 --> 00:54:27,645
if the opposite
happens, we will support them.

567
00:54:28,365 --> 00:54:30,525
We'll take Orhan Bey out, brothers.

568
00:54:32,185 --> 00:54:34,895
Doesn't Osman Bey
fear for the lives of his children?

569
00:54:35,665 --> 00:54:41,515
A wolf that does not have a scar
on its neck is not considered a wolf.

570
00:54:43,265 --> 00:54:44,975
You're right, Aykurt.

571
00:54:50,475 --> 00:54:52,975
You say you took every precaution.

572
00:54:53,755 --> 00:54:56,065
Well, what about Nayman?
What does he want from Orhan?

573
00:54:56,285 --> 00:54:59,775
He treated him first and now, he
is completing what he did.

574
00:55:00,105 --> 00:55:01,845
So what does he want?

575
00:55:02,065 --> 00:55:06,605
He wants Orhan for the same reason
he wants me.

576
00:55:10,015 --> 00:55:13,055
His intention isn't to diminish the
number of those who are against him.

577
00:55:13,075 --> 00:55:15,405
Rather, to increase the
number of those in his class.

578
00:55:15,435 --> 00:55:19,625
He couldn't bring me to his side and
now he wants to take advantage of Orhan.

579
00:55:24,395 --> 00:55:26,175
And what do you want, my Bey?

580
00:55:27,035 --> 00:55:29,455
Orhan will open his ears and eyes well.

581
00:55:32,305 --> 00:55:34,305
I know part of Nayman's plan.

582
00:55:35,145 --> 00:55:37,165
And Orhan will do the rest.

583
00:55:38,875 --> 00:55:42,605
Just as the buds of our country are
transformed into a mighty tree.

584
00:55:45,615 --> 00:55:48,115
What you say is nice, however...

585
00:55:48,685 --> 00:55:51,205
What if something worse
happened to Orhan?

586
00:55:52,465 --> 00:55:53,825
Tell me.

587
00:55:54,975 --> 00:55:57,025
When I was at Nayman's headquarters...

588
00:55:57,465 --> 00:55:59,505
Were you both freaking out like that?

589
00:56:04,745 --> 00:56:06,745
They treated Orhan the same way.

590
00:56:07,465 --> 00:56:09,965
Since he will follow the
example of his ancestors...

591
00:56:10,235 --> 00:56:15,305
Orhan will also walk the
thorny paths that we passed.

592
00:56:15,915 --> 00:56:17,285
Don't worry.

593
00:56:17,385 --> 00:56:19,275
He will come back safely.

594
00:56:19,335 --> 00:56:21,505
Like the wolf attacks the lamb...

595
00:56:22,105 --> 00:56:24,405
he will attack and get
out of there safely.

596
00:56:29,145 --> 00:56:30,485
And now...

597
00:56:31,885 --> 00:56:33,135
there is another...

598
00:56:34,145 --> 00:56:36,035
important thing.

599
00:56:36,895 --> 00:56:39,085
Tell Bengi Hatun and ask her to come.

600
00:56:40,875 --> 00:56:43,375
Let's have iftaar together.

601
00:56:44,175 --> 00:56:46,335
And let's talk about the
thing that is incomplete.

602
00:56:53,945 --> 00:56:55,285
Come on.

603
00:57:45,195 --> 00:57:49,985
You and those with you will ask
my father for mercy, Nayman.

604
00:57:53,245 --> 00:57:54,595
Hurry up.

605
00:57:54,965 --> 00:57:56,835
We'll load it all into Bayındır's cart.

606
00:57:57,035 --> 00:57:58,175
Come on!

607
00:59:38,955 --> 00:59:41,475
Söğüt

608
00:59:48,295 --> 00:59:50,435
Bayındır!

609
00:59:52,065 --> 00:59:57,115
He had the courage to betray me.

610
00:59:59,055 --> 01:00:04,555
What is the penalty for betraying me...

611
01:00:04,865 --> 01:00:06,405
Celali?

612
01:00:07,875 --> 01:00:11,375
To lose what he loves most, Mother Sultan.

613
01:00:13,585 --> 01:00:17,035
I'll catch him.

614
01:00:18,495 --> 01:00:22,315
First I'll take the document
from his hand...

615
01:00:23,395 --> 01:00:24,725
and then...

616
01:00:25,885 --> 01:00:27,225
his money...

617
01:00:28,555 --> 01:00:30,065
and then....

618
01:00:40,095 --> 01:00:41,415
his life.

619
01:00:50,785 --> 01:00:52,815
As long as he has armor like Nayman...

620
01:00:52,915 --> 01:00:56,735
catching him
certainly won't be easy.

621
01:00:59,375 --> 01:01:01,965
However, I will do something that...

622
01:01:04,315 --> 01:01:06,515
What shall we do, Mother Sultan?

623
01:01:15,265 --> 01:01:18,275
Allah is great!

624
01:01:18,475 --> 01:01:22,195
First, we will break our fast, Celali.

625
01:01:27,315 --> 01:01:30,275
I bear witness that there
is no deity but Allah...

626
01:01:30,475 --> 01:01:33,035
Yenişehir, Osman Bey's palace.

627
01:01:33,115 --> 01:01:34,705
I bear witness that there
is no deity but Allah...

628
01:01:34,825 --> 01:01:38,195
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

629
01:01:38,545 --> 01:01:40,405
O Possessor of majesty and honor.

630
01:01:40,795 --> 01:01:45,155
We thank you for getting us to have
the blessed Ramadan.

631
01:01:45,405 --> 01:01:48,965
Amin.

632
01:01:49,335 --> 01:01:54,525
We know that prayers come from
fasting mouths at the iftaar table...

633
01:01:54,625 --> 01:01:57,005
is important.

634
01:01:58,225 --> 01:02:02,305
Oh my Allah, the Most
Gracious, the Most Merciful.

635
01:02:02,415 --> 01:02:07,355
Unite all Muslims under
the banner of Islam.

636
01:02:07,375 --> 01:02:09,375
Amin.

637
01:02:09,875 --> 01:02:17,215
Make us the back on which the oppressed rely
and the city that terrorizes the oppressors!

638
01:02:17,295 --> 01:02:19,295
Amin.

639
01:02:20,365 --> 01:02:22,255
We are powerless.

640
01:02:22,455 --> 01:02:24,455
Get us together.

641
01:02:24,525 --> 01:02:29,075
Heal all our diseases that
are in our bodies and souls.

642
01:02:29,085 --> 01:02:31,085
Amin.

643
01:02:31,235 --> 01:02:34,015
Oh my Allah.

644
01:02:34,815 --> 01:02:39,295
In the blessed Ramadan, all devils are chained up.

645
01:02:39,695 --> 01:02:42,975
But our souls are with us.

646
01:02:43,375 --> 01:02:48,945
Save us from obeying ourselves
and indulging in sin.

647
01:02:49,115 --> 01:02:51,515
Amin.

648
01:02:52,315 --> 01:03:00,225
Grant us good obedience in Ramadan,
and let us reach Eid with goodness.

649
01:03:00,335 --> 01:03:02,015
Amin.

650
01:03:18,285 --> 01:03:19,815
May Allah accept our fasts.

651
01:03:20,075 --> 01:03:21,555
Come on, enjoy your meal.

652
01:03:21,575 --> 01:03:25,295
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

653
01:03:26,335 --> 01:03:30,085
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

654
01:03:35,855 --> 01:03:37,395
Go ahead.

655
01:03:39,795 --> 01:03:43,125
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

656
01:03:49,535 --> 01:03:51,125
Oh.

657
01:04:04,555 --> 01:04:06,655
Praise be to Allah, thank you very much.

658
01:04:10,635 --> 01:04:12,525
We broke our fast.

659
01:04:13,405 --> 01:04:18,515
Thank Allah that my son did his job
and made it to our iftaar.

660
01:04:23,455 --> 01:04:25,585
As we broke our fasts....

661
01:04:26,125 --> 01:04:29,325
tell us, son.

662
01:04:31,485 --> 01:04:33,645
What's happening in Nayman's around?

663
01:04:34,015 --> 01:04:35,355
My Bey.

664
01:04:35,855 --> 01:04:39,645
What I heard and saw
hurt my soul.

665
01:04:40,945 --> 01:04:43,715
Those who are on our
side are betraying us.

666
01:04:46,115 --> 01:04:47,635
Bayındır Bey.

667
01:04:49,315 --> 01:04:50,665
What's his campaign?

668
01:04:51,235 --> 01:04:53,825
Bayındır Bey will go to
Talay to take the seal.

669
01:04:53,965 --> 01:04:56,535
Soldiers will unite in Akçaağaç.

670
01:04:57,435 --> 01:04:59,115
If Nayman has the seal...

671
01:04:59,205 --> 01:05:04,395
he will put it on our death firman.

672
01:05:09,985 --> 01:05:12,755
Never worry, we won't allow that.

673
01:05:15,025 --> 01:05:16,915
Bayindir only cares about the gold.

674
01:05:17,375 --> 01:05:18,915
This is expected of him.

675
01:05:18,915 --> 01:05:22,045
...but Vizier Saveli.

676
01:05:22,865 --> 01:05:24,735
He also serves Nayman.

677
01:05:25,775 --> 01:05:27,315
Is he so?

678
01:05:33,025 --> 01:05:34,765
As long as...

679
01:05:35,745 --> 01:05:38,805
...such people only care about their profits
instead of helping...

680
01:05:40,805 --> 01:05:43,075
...they will keep experiencing my punishment.

681
01:05:46,045 --> 01:05:47,935
What shall we do now, my Bey?

682
01:05:48,175 --> 01:05:51,425
We will not stop until we bury them!

683
01:05:56,885 --> 01:05:58,765
Now let's come to the main question.

684
01:06:10,735 --> 01:06:14,235
Orhan heard everything.

685
01:06:16,735 --> 01:06:22,755
And he will tell Osman that you will go
through the location of the White Tree

686
01:06:24,655 --> 01:06:26,005
That's good.

687
01:06:27,855 --> 01:06:29,565
I will not take that way.

688
01:06:33,405 --> 01:06:35,715
Your brain works, merchant.

689
01:06:38,385 --> 01:06:41,645
You will go through Kurtagzi.

690
01:06:41,935 --> 01:06:43,315
...and I...

691
01:06:43,345 --> 01:06:45,345
I will be at the White Tree location.

692
01:06:45,605 --> 01:06:47,935
I will kill Osman there.

693
01:06:53,235 --> 01:06:55,755
Commander Nayman, Orhan knows about me.

694
01:06:56,655 --> 01:06:58,525
What happens if he tells Osman?

695
01:07:01,615 --> 01:07:03,725
Vizier of the supreme Seljuq state.

696
01:07:04,355 --> 01:07:07,215
Are you afraid of a Bey, huh?

697
01:07:09,215 --> 01:07:12,225
When you arrive in Konya.

698
01:07:13,135 --> 01:07:15,225
Osman will be dead.

699
01:07:19,985 --> 01:07:23,165
Commander Nayman, what mission
aer you giving me in Konya?

700
01:07:23,795 --> 01:07:28,595
You will behead Sultan Aladdin.

701
01:07:29,395 --> 01:07:32,995
And you will hang it on
the highest place in Konya

702
01:07:35,365 --> 01:07:38,595
There will be no one left to prevent this.

703
01:07:40,225 --> 01:07:43,315
The seal will come and
we will establish the state

704
01:07:53,425 --> 01:07:55,135
Tell me, son.

705
01:07:56,565 --> 01:07:58,265
How did you get out of there?

706
01:07:59,705 --> 01:08:01,495
They were carrying goods, my Bey.

707
01:08:01,495 --> 01:08:03,015
I hid among them.

708
01:08:03,365 --> 01:08:04,675
So...

709
01:08:05,455 --> 01:08:07,495
Wasn't there a soldier guarding you?

710
01:08:16,524 --> 01:08:18,045
No, my Bey.

711
01:08:24,115 --> 01:08:25,425
Son.

712
01:08:28,255 --> 01:08:30,285
So you didn't run away from there.

713
01:08:33,085 --> 01:08:35,145
They let you go.

714
01:08:40,685 --> 01:08:43,225
So what you heard is suspicious.

715
01:08:45,665 --> 01:08:48,404
Are you saying that
what Orhan heard was a lie?

716
01:08:48,404 --> 01:08:50,404
No, the traitors are known.

717
01:08:50,495 --> 01:08:52,505
...the traitors are known, however...

718
01:08:54,734 --> 01:08:57,825
The location of the white tree must be a trap.

719
01:09:03,375 --> 01:09:05,415
They want to drag us there.

720
01:09:07,165 --> 01:09:09,715
But we will hit them where they least expect it.

721
01:09:12,104 --> 01:09:15,185
We will set such an ambush that...

722
01:09:20,135 --> 01:09:22,505
Do you mean I have failed
in my mission, my Bey?

723
01:09:22,505 --> 01:09:25,154
No, you have done your job perfectly.

724
01:09:26,234 --> 01:09:30,535
If Nayman hadn't called you in,
our plan would have been obvious.

725
01:09:32,285 --> 01:09:33,929
And if you had not gotten out...

726
01:09:33,929 --> 01:09:37,809
there would have been 500 horsemen
waiting for you in front of the headquarters.

727
01:09:37,809 --> 01:09:40,305
Son, you went and saw.

728
01:09:41,205 --> 01:09:47,135
Now it is time to defeat him.

729
01:09:49,154 --> 01:09:50,734
Thank you, my Bey.

730
01:09:54,234 --> 01:09:56,085
How do we defeat them, my Bey?

731
01:09:57,005 --> 01:10:01,355
We will suffer very heavy losses in
any war we wage in the field.

732
01:10:01,355 --> 01:10:04,885
For this reason, we will launch
another campaign against them.

733
01:10:08,205 --> 01:10:10,005
Is it a secret, my Bey?

734
01:10:11,535 --> 01:10:14,585
The secret will be revealed
when the time comes.

735
01:10:22,435 --> 01:10:25,485
Son, tell me, how is your hand?

736
01:10:33,435 --> 01:10:37,455
It's fine, father.
What he did was beneficial, thank Allah.

737
01:10:38,685 --> 01:10:40,255
Thank Allah.

738
01:10:45,255 --> 01:10:47,455
Now let's cut to the main problem.

739
01:11:02,505 --> 01:11:08,185
Now it's time for
Aktemur and Alcicek to tie the knot.

740
01:11:12,885 --> 01:11:14,705
Do the preparations.

741
01:11:39,835 --> 01:11:46,105
Enter all of Bayindir's
secret warehouses and stores.

742
01:11:48,285 --> 01:11:50,305
I will set the seal on this matter.

743
01:11:52,285 --> 01:11:54,605
Will you let me in, Mother Sultan?

744
01:11:54,655 --> 01:11:56,035
Enter!

745
01:12:00,105 --> 01:12:02,655
It's from Osman Bey, ma'am.

746
01:12:21,255 --> 01:12:26,285
Osman bey calls me to
Yenisehir at dawn.

747
01:12:29,155 --> 01:12:30,605
He says it is important.

748
01:12:36,185 --> 01:12:39,555
What are you planning again, Osman?

749
01:12:42,805 --> 01:12:44,835
- Do you accept?
- I do.

750
01:12:45,705 --> 01:12:48,585
- Do you accept?
- I do.

751
01:12:56,585 --> 01:12:58,635
Aktemur, Gunduz Bey's son...

752
01:13:00,905 --> 01:13:08,185
Will you marry Alcicek, daughter
of Oktem Bey, with the dowry you promised her?

753
01:13:10,305 --> 01:13:11,685
Yes.

754
01:13:12,005 --> 01:13:14,885
- Do you accept?
- I do.

755
01:13:15,935 --> 01:13:19,255
- Do you accept?
- I do.

756
01:13:25,485 --> 01:13:28,905
And you witnesses, do you bear witness to this?

757
01:13:29,235 --> 01:13:31,255
- We do.
- We do.

758
01:13:31,885 --> 01:13:33,255
We do.

759
01:13:35,655 --> 01:13:38,385
May Allah bless your future.

760
01:13:39,185 --> 01:13:41,185
- Amen.
- Amen.

761
01:13:51,955 --> 01:13:57,705
Oh my Allah, we witnessed
the marriage of these two young people.

762
01:13:58,635 --> 01:14:00,185
You shall testify.

763
01:14:00,735 --> 01:14:03,805
Bless their marriage.

764
01:14:03,805 --> 01:14:05,555
- Amen.
- Amen.

765
01:14:05,555 --> 01:14:13,135
Grant this couple understanding,
love and stability in their marriage

766
01:14:13,135 --> 01:14:14,505
- Amen.
- Amen.

767
01:14:14,735 --> 01:14:20,305
Do not create a place for misunderstanding,
hatred or separation between them.

768
01:14:20,305 --> 01:14:22,305
- Amen.
- Amen.

769
01:14:22,955 --> 01:14:24,585
Al-Fatiha

770
01:14:44,635 --> 01:14:46,705
In the name of Allah,
the most gracious, the most merciful

771
01:14:47,155 --> 01:14:49,235
In the name of Allah,
the most gracious, the most merciful

772
01:15:12,085 --> 01:15:13,435
Son.

773
01:15:38,835 --> 01:15:42,905
This was for my brother, the martyr, Gunduz Bey.
I put it in your trust now.

774
01:15:43,055 --> 01:15:44,605
Take it.

775
01:15:56,235 --> 01:15:58,965
In the name of Allah,
the most gracious, the most merciful

776
01:16:11,355 --> 01:16:12,855
Alps!

777
01:16:13,835 --> 01:16:16,135
Draw your swords!

778
01:16:16,455 --> 01:16:18,755
Your command, my Bey!

779
01:17:33,455 --> 01:17:35,785
What did Aktemur Bey do?

780
01:17:35,785 --> 01:17:39,785
He held wedding and banquet

781
01:17:39,885 --> 01:17:42,905
What did he do for Alcicek Hatun?

782
01:17:42,905 --> 01:17:49,535
He slaughtered calfs
and sheep for her

783
01:17:49,535 --> 01:17:52,935
Did he break a heart or say a bad word?

784
01:17:52,935 --> 01:17:56,205
He did neither break hearts
nor say a bad word

785
01:17:56,205 --> 01:17:59,805
And he married to Alcicek Hautn!

786
01:17:59,805 --> 01:18:03,605
So, Allah bless them

787
01:18:03,605 --> 01:18:04,955
Amen

788
01:18:05,055 --> 01:18:07,055
May you both be happy!

789
01:18:07,055 --> 01:18:09,635
Sleep on one pillow!

790
01:18:14,585 --> 01:18:16,585
You stop, you stop.

791
01:18:16,905 --> 01:18:18,655
Brother stop here.

792
01:18:21,055 --> 01:18:23,135
- Let's do it.
- Let's do it.

793
01:18:28,035 --> 01:18:30,555
Strike, Gurbuz Alp!

794
01:18:33,185 --> 01:18:34,685
Come on!

795
01:18:44,135 --> 01:18:48,135
You are next, Cerkutay.

796
01:18:48,485 --> 01:18:52,555
He will see marriage in his dreams.

797
01:18:52,855 --> 01:18:57,335
I heard, I heard,
but this time you bumped into a solid rock!

798
01:18:57,335 --> 01:19:00,855
What a rock huh!

799
01:19:00,855 --> 01:19:03,755
Look, he can't even stand
without his shield!

800
01:19:05,835 --> 01:19:07,585
Alps!

801
01:19:09,255 --> 01:19:10,635
Stop!

802
01:19:11,205 --> 01:19:12,555
Stop.

803
01:19:19,085 --> 01:19:20,605
Don't do this.

804
01:19:22,655 --> 01:19:24,355
Come to your senses.

805
01:19:29,785 --> 01:19:33,335
Go rest, there's a war tomorrow!

806
01:19:33,635 --> 01:19:35,405
We are in difficulty!

807
01:19:44,035 --> 01:19:45,585
Alps!

808
01:19:52,285 --> 01:19:55,005
What is this lunatic doing here?

809
01:19:55,005 --> 01:19:56,705
Lunatic?
Who?

810
01:19:56,805 --> 01:19:59,335
I'm lunatic! I am!

811
01:20:00,805 --> 01:20:04,335
She's talking about our lunatic, Cerkutay!

812
01:20:04,335 --> 01:20:08,355
He's roaming here thanks to
the mercy of Osman bey.

813
01:20:08,355 --> 01:20:10,905
We give him some soup
and send him away.

814
01:20:16,205 --> 01:20:17,705
Get out of my way.

815
01:20:23,805 --> 01:20:25,505
He's very coward.

816
01:20:26,185 --> 01:20:28,705
Stop it, don't be afraid, I'll look at your head.

817
01:20:34,245 --> 01:20:36,815
Stop.
Good, good.

818
01:20:39,285 --> 01:20:42,205
I hit you well, bless my hands.

819
01:20:42,885 --> 01:20:44,255
Ulgen!

820
01:20:44,285 --> 01:20:45,605
Yes mother?

821
01:20:45,605 --> 01:20:48,135
Give this lunatic oinment.

822
01:20:48,735 --> 01:20:50,105
I will.

823
01:20:51,135 --> 01:20:53,935
If I'd known he was a lunatic,
I wouldn't have hit him.

824
01:20:54,055 --> 01:20:56,505
Lunatic, lunatic, lunatic!

825
01:21:02,655 --> 01:21:05,205
You did well, very well.

826
01:21:05,735 --> 01:21:08,655
Look, he came to his senses.

827
01:21:08,655 --> 01:21:10,655
He is blooming.

828
01:21:11,605 --> 01:21:13,305
Let me kiss your hand.

829
01:21:16,405 --> 01:21:17,905
What tribe are you from?

830
01:21:17,905 --> 01:21:19,435
- I?
- Yes!

831
01:21:23,385 --> 01:21:24,755
I am from...

832
01:21:25,485 --> 01:21:26,805
Are you married?

833
01:21:26,805 --> 01:21:27,555
Married?

834
01:21:27,555 --> 01:21:31,835
Mother, mother come on,
let's take you to your room

835
01:21:35,555 --> 01:21:37,085
Let's go.

836
01:21:42,595 --> 01:21:45,145
-Is she her mother?
-Yes

837
01:21:49,855 --> 01:21:51,185
Brother.

838
01:21:51,805 --> 01:21:53,135
Look.

839
01:21:54,885 --> 01:21:57,905
You've crossed many obstacles
in your life, Cerkutay.

840
01:21:59,355 --> 01:22:02,005
But now you are in a very
difficult position, brother.

841
01:22:08,185 --> 01:22:11,905
Yes I am, I am doomed.

842
01:22:12,485 --> 01:22:14,855
I can't walk around without a shield anymore.

843
01:22:16,055 --> 01:22:18,605
What happened to the double swords, Cerkutay?

844
01:22:21,735 --> 01:22:25,805
The mansion has become
more dangerous than the battlefield.

845
01:22:26,585 --> 01:22:28,455
May Allah help me.

846
01:22:30,155 --> 01:22:33,835
Allah helps the lunatic, brother.

847
01:22:34,785 --> 01:22:38,335
I've had enough of you!
Enough of you!

848
01:22:43,050 --> 01:22:45,755
Yenisehir

849
01:22:47,435 --> 01:22:49,935
That Nayman... his name is Nayman, right?

850
01:22:50,035 --> 01:22:53,755
If the place he mentioned to Bayindir
is a trap, so are we going twords a trap?

851
01:22:53,755 --> 01:22:55,435
What's it, brother?

852
01:22:57,735 --> 01:22:59,605
Are you afraid, Cerkutay.

853
01:22:59,985 --> 01:23:04,485
Let me ask you,
have you ever seen Cerkutay scared?

854
01:23:05,185 --> 01:23:08,905
If we hadn't seen that you were afraid of
the brown midwife, we would have believed it

855
01:23:12,615 --> 01:23:15,885
I doubt the mind of those who are not afraid of it

856
01:23:15,885 --> 01:23:18,165
Don't mention her name in front of me

857
01:23:25,805 --> 01:23:30,085
By Allah , brother, if only that
brown midwife had hit you a little harder

858
01:23:30,115 --> 01:23:33,685
I would be in a worse position than,
Allah forbid, the lunatic you imitated

859
01:23:37,335 --> 01:23:40,185
Look at the warriors, at the warriors

860
01:23:40,185 --> 01:23:42,185
Look at their tongues

861
01:23:42,765 --> 01:23:46,115
Your mouths do more work than your hands

862
01:23:46,315 --> 01:23:53,135
Boran Alp didn't take care of you while I was
a spy in Ingol, brothers

863
01:23:55,335 --> 01:23:57,335
How did I not take care of them, brother?

864
01:24:02,305 --> 01:24:04,555
Also, wasn't Osman Bey saying

865
01:24:04,585 --> 01:24:08,175
We're notorious for intrigue,
didn't he say that?

866
01:24:12,985 --> 01:24:17,015
That means he said it at a time when
you weren't listening, Cerkutay.

867
01:24:18,865 --> 01:24:23,085
Brother, brother, I do not hear.

868
01:24:32,885 --> 01:24:39,915
I pray that no one will sign your tongues.

869
01:24:43,765 --> 01:24:47,265
Brother, really, what are we going to do?

870
01:24:49,385 --> 01:24:50,985
And I don't know, brother

871
01:24:51,785 --> 01:24:54,635
But I know we're going to
hit Nayman hard.

872
01:24:58,465 --> 01:24:59,985
powerful hit.

873
01:25:00,085 --> 01:25:01,935
Yes, big hit

874
01:25:07,285 --> 01:25:08,785
Warriors!

875
01:25:09,915 --> 01:25:11,415
Dear brothers!

876
01:25:12,935 --> 01:25:14,635
Brave ones!

877
01:25:16,035 --> 01:25:17,565
We will unite!

878
01:25:19,435 --> 01:25:21,465
And we will unite.

879
01:25:24,365 --> 01:25:25,935
Then that Nayman--

880
01:25:26,015 --> 01:25:28,015
-Nayman, isn't it?
-Yes.

881
01:25:29,335 --> 01:25:32,765
We're going to hit Nayman hard!

882
01:25:33,815 --> 01:25:36,865
Attention, Osman Bey!

883
01:25:40,885 --> 01:25:43,615
Warriors, heroes!

884
01:25:46,115 --> 01:25:48,835
If you are going to fight
soldiers from hell...

885
01:25:49,585 --> 01:25:52,635
Then you should not allow them
to enter heaven.

886
01:25:55,485 --> 01:25:57,365
But we will do the opposite.

887
01:25:58,515 --> 01:26:00,235
Close the doors.

888
01:26:00,335 --> 01:26:01,915
Line up the spears.

889
01:26:02,365 --> 01:26:04,785
You will set traps everywhere.

890
01:26:04,785 --> 01:26:07,885
You'll put explosives everywhere.

891
01:26:09,185 --> 01:26:13,135
We'll root Nayman out of
our heavenly home.

892
01:26:13,435 --> 01:26:17,015
Come on, everyone spread out
all over Yenişehir.

893
01:26:17,015 --> 01:26:18,385
Your command, sir.

894
01:26:18,385 --> 01:26:19,965
Yes sir.

895
01:26:19,965 --> 01:26:21,465
My lord!

896
01:26:25,565 --> 01:26:27,285
The Queen Mother is coming

897
01:26:33,645 --> 01:26:34,975
Come on.

898
01:26:35,705 --> 01:26:37,595
Come on, everyone back to work.

899
01:28:08,505 --> 01:28:11,295
Forgive me, Great Commander Nayman.

900
01:28:18,075 --> 01:28:22,365
You don't deserve forgiveness, blacksmith.

901
01:28:22,925 --> 01:28:25,235
But we'll see...

902
01:28:25,235 --> 01:28:30,235
if your sword is sharp,
you will die quickly.

903
01:28:30,765 --> 01:28:32,545
If not...

904
01:28:35,425 --> 01:28:37,435
Forgive me, Great Commander Neiman.

905
01:28:37,435 --> 01:28:38,965
Pardon me.

906
01:28:43,295 --> 01:28:46,025
Forgive me, Great Commander Nayman.

907
01:29:13,175 --> 01:29:16,745
How will I defeat the enemy with
his likes...

908
01:29:17,175 --> 01:29:19,755
which is not doing its job properly?

909
01:29:20,205 --> 01:29:22,405
He will pay with his life.

910
01:29:26,905 --> 01:29:30,455
Take that sword.

911
01:29:30,575 --> 01:29:36,155
I will slowly decapitate Osman with it.

912
01:29:44,125 --> 01:29:48,065
Osman is now walking toward
the trap I set for him.

913
01:29:48,285 --> 01:29:51,055
This will end today.

914
01:29:51,175 --> 01:29:55,265
After the fall of Osman,
everything will be as I want.

915
01:29:57,515 --> 01:30:03,255
The blood that will be spilled on
this earth will serve our purpose.

916
01:30:09,405 --> 01:30:12,705
Draw your swords.

917
01:30:13,485 --> 01:30:15,595
Ride the horses.

918
01:30:15,805 --> 01:30:20,595
We're going to the site of the White Tree
to behead Osman.

919
01:30:20,785 --> 01:30:24,895
Today is the day of Arlik Khan's wrath.

920
01:30:25,085 --> 01:30:32,665
Arlik Khan! Arlik Khan!

921
01:30:32,995 --> 01:30:41,005
This time isn't like the times we went to
Sogut, nor the times we went to Ingol.

922
01:30:41,725 --> 01:30:47,675
Check the chariots and men well now.

923
01:30:48,455 --> 01:30:49,985
Our way is long.

924
01:30:50,025 --> 01:30:52,455
We have to be ready.

925
01:30:52,455 --> 01:30:54,635
Everything is ready, sir.

926
01:30:55,055 --> 01:30:57,105
Warriors are very strong.

927
01:30:57,105 --> 01:31:00,315
We took with us the strongest
and most dexterous of them.

928
01:31:01,795 --> 01:31:04,045
Good. Good.

929
01:31:04,465 --> 01:31:10,355
The road ahead is very long, Hussein.

930
01:31:11,125 --> 01:31:14,575
We'll go from here now...

931
01:31:16,105 --> 01:31:18,985
but our return will be very different.

932
01:31:19,415 --> 01:31:30,925
You will see that I open one court and
close another in Yenişehir Palace.

933
01:31:33,255 --> 01:31:36,095
It suits you, sir, it suits you very much.

934
01:31:36,915 --> 01:31:39,425
Definitely befitting.

935
01:31:41,245 --> 01:31:43,255
Definitely befitting.

936
01:31:54,815 --> 01:31:57,155
Come on, hurry up, come on.

937
01:32:02,615 --> 01:32:05,265
Get the horses quick, come on.

938
01:32:05,515 --> 01:32:08,575
Warriors, come on.

939
01:32:13,185 --> 01:32:16,405
They spent all day at camp .

940
01:32:16,725 --> 01:32:21,275
Then they began collecting goods
before the call to prayer.

941
01:32:24,575 --> 01:32:26,465
Look at his condition.

942
01:32:28,415 --> 01:32:31,995
Walk with a little more pride,
Bayindir Bey.

943
01:32:32,285 --> 01:32:34,565
The time will surely come.

944
01:32:35,145 --> 01:32:37,695
And we'll quell your arrogance, too.

945
01:32:38,525 --> 01:32:41,105
My mission ends here, Turgut Bey.

946
01:32:41,805 --> 01:32:45,395
I have to go back to Osman Bey's side,
may Allah help you.

947
01:32:45,815 --> 01:32:48,325
May Allah help us all, my brother.

948
01:32:48,485 --> 01:32:49,995
Thank you.

949
01:32:56,585 --> 01:32:59,965
What shall we do now, sir?
What are you thinking?

950
01:33:07,865 --> 01:33:09,935
Let this fox out on the road...

951
01:33:10,185 --> 01:33:12,875
There's definitely something
I'm thinking of.

952
01:33:13,355 --> 01:33:15,125
Shall we hit him and leave him?

953
01:33:15,865 --> 01:33:17,205
No.

954
01:33:17,425 --> 01:33:21,145
First, we will observe him as
his shadow step by step

955
01:33:21,145 --> 01:33:26,365
And then he will bring that
precious seal to us with his feet.

956
01:33:27,455 --> 01:33:29,025
Alright, sir.

957
01:33:29,215 --> 01:33:31,755
Your time is now, Bayindir.

958
01:33:58,825 --> 01:34:01,975
Since when do the elders come to
the younger, Osman Bey?

959
01:34:03,375 --> 01:34:05,075
You summoned me.

960
01:34:08,675 --> 01:34:11,045
If you were come to hold me accountable

961
01:34:12,675 --> 01:34:14,685
you would come without thinking that.

962
01:34:17,015 --> 01:34:19,475
What is the reason for
the preparations outside?

963
01:34:20,045 --> 01:34:22,195
It is for the doom of the infidels.

964
01:34:23,525 --> 01:34:25,055
Never worry.

965
01:34:28,515 --> 01:34:31,035
Tell me without further ado,
Osman Bey.

966
01:34:38,025 --> 01:34:39,525
Vizier Saveli.

967
01:34:43,405 --> 01:34:48,485
He's been working for Commander Nayman
since day one.

968
01:34:52,685 --> 01:34:56,505
Grand Vizier of the House of Seljuk!
How could this happen?

969
01:34:58,115 --> 01:35:00,175
While I was at headquarters that day...

970
01:35:01,055 --> 01:35:05,055
even your closest soldiers kneeled
before Nayman

971
01:35:07,275 --> 01:35:09,075
You've seen that.

972
01:35:11,465 --> 01:35:13,545
Never be surprised by Vizie Saveli.

973
01:35:19,405 --> 01:35:21,975
My son?

974
01:35:25,595 --> 01:35:28,495
Vizier Savel is the closest
person to Sultan Aladdin.

975
01:35:30,645 --> 01:35:32,705
The Sultan's life is in danger.

976
01:35:33,485 --> 01:35:36,075
I will go to Konya without
wasting time, Osman Bey.

977
01:35:37,295 --> 01:35:38,595
Stop.

978
01:35:42,225 --> 01:35:43,525
Stop.

979
01:35:47,045 --> 01:35:48,545
You are right.

980
01:35:53,245 --> 01:35:59,515
Konya and Sultan
Alaeddin are also in danger.

981
01:36:01,675 --> 01:36:06,045
But if you go, you'll be in danger too.

982
01:36:08,135 --> 01:36:10,605
And what do you advise me, Osman Bey?

983
01:36:13,525 --> 01:36:15,525
(Oktam tribe)

984
01:36:26,250 --> 01:36:27,750
welcome

985
01:36:28,480 --> 01:36:30,560
You were welcome and you were easy

986
01:36:37,840 --> 01:36:39,340
Welcome!

987
01:36:43,820 --> 01:36:49,840
Welcome!

988
01:37:34,485 --> 01:37:36,535
You both came at the right time.

989
01:37:36,745 --> 01:37:38,135
My daughter.

990
01:37:43,905 --> 01:37:45,205
My son.

991
01:37:50,995 --> 01:37:52,795
Welcome to your home.

992
01:37:58,565 --> 01:38:00,385
I have prepared your tent.

993
01:38:01,035 --> 01:38:03,095
There is nothing missing for you anymore.

994
01:38:05,135 --> 01:38:06,435
Tent?

995
01:38:08,425 --> 01:38:10,125
And where did you get this from?

996
01:38:12,565 --> 01:38:16,135
They'll stay at the palace, Bengu Hatun.

997
01:38:18,565 --> 01:38:20,565
They came here to kiss your hand.

998
01:38:26,085 --> 01:38:28,105
What's going on, Bengu Hatun?

999
01:38:28,405 --> 01:38:30,435
Tell us what you want to say now.

1000
01:38:33,405 --> 01:38:35,265
Aktemur lives in the palace.

1001
01:38:35,825 --> 01:38:38,645
And the place Alcicek is with her husband.

1002
01:38:46,705 --> 01:38:50,255
Or are you thinking of something
we don't know about?

1003
01:38:51,235 --> 01:38:55,265
There's nothing to hide,
I said what I wanted from the start

1004
01:38:57,185 --> 01:38:58,985
Isn't it, son?

1005
01:39:04,755 --> 01:39:07,255
What's going on, Aktemur?

1006
01:39:20,995 --> 01:39:23,045
You will not go alone, Queen Mother

1007
01:39:27,775 --> 01:39:29,275
We'll go together

1008
01:39:30,795 --> 01:39:36,315
I will never forget the one who got me
through the hard times, Bala Hatun.

1009
01:39:38,945 --> 01:39:40,445
May Allah bless you.

1010
01:39:41,675 --> 01:39:45,685
We also wanted someone to support us in
difficult times, not the other way around.

1011
01:39:45,905 --> 01:39:47,955
We also do not forget, Sultana Mother

1012
01:39:51,525 --> 01:39:54,535
But today is a day for unity.

1013
01:39:57,235 --> 01:39:59,815
We have to go without
wasting any more time.

1014
01:40:03,205 --> 01:40:05,205
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey.

1015
01:40:05,945 --> 01:40:08,505
May Allah make your way easy,
Sultana Mother

1016
01:40:18,935 --> 01:40:20,235
Bala.

1017
01:40:21,855 --> 01:40:24,915
Saveli realizes that Orhan
knows he's a traitor.

1018
01:40:25,775 --> 01:40:27,865
And that we go there as enemies.

1019
01:40:28,305 --> 01:40:31,845
For this reason, you should be careful.

1020
01:40:32,355 --> 01:40:35,155
Don't worry, my dear Osman,
and you, too, be careful.

1021
01:40:36,425 --> 01:40:38,435
Say that we will fight the infidels
with our swords together.

1022
01:40:39,095 --> 01:40:41,115
They will not leave us alone.

1023
01:40:41,575 --> 01:40:43,595
We will not stop fighting them either.

1024
01:40:45,555 --> 01:40:47,075
May Allah bless our battle..

1025
01:40:50,795 --> 01:40:52,325
We will return victorious.

1026
01:40:52,535 --> 01:40:55,125
And we will see your victory when
we return too, Allah willing.

1027
01:40:55,945 --> 01:40:57,725
May Allah make your path easy.

1028
01:41:08,775 --> 01:41:10,315
Bengu Hatun.

1029
01:41:12,025 --> 01:41:13,765
Why did the beys gather?

1030
01:41:14,585 --> 01:41:16,605
A meeting will be held to select the bey.

1031
01:41:18,985 --> 01:41:23,835
Today I will hand over the position to the
lord of the Kargin tribe.

1032
01:41:26,365 --> 01:41:32,045
And my son-in-law Aktemur
will be made lord of the Kargin tribe.

1033
01:41:38,445 --> 01:41:40,655
And he will receive Öktem's trust.

1034
01:41:42,105 --> 01:41:44,685
Say something, Aktemur.

1035
01:41:49,625 --> 01:41:56,715
Bengi Hatun...
Mother Bengi wants this.

1036
01:41:59,565 --> 01:42:02,005
And I learned that from Alcicek yesterday.

1037
01:42:05,875 --> 01:42:08,005
But I haven't made up my mind yet.

1038
01:42:11,005 --> 01:42:13,015
What are you knitting again, Bengi Hatun?

1039
01:42:13,585 --> 01:42:16,175
How could you do this
without Osman Bey's knowledge?

1040
01:42:16,665 --> 01:42:18,665
Isn't everything we've lived enough?

1041
01:42:19,825 --> 01:42:21,825
No game, Aunt Malhun.

1042
01:42:22,095 --> 01:42:26,425
My mother will hand over
my father's trust to Aktemur.

1043
01:42:29,545 --> 01:42:31,835
What is the point of being
angry about this?

1044
01:42:31,905 --> 01:42:34,715
Also, why would Osman Bey object?

1045
01:42:37,855 --> 01:42:40,635
So, you're okay with that
too, Alcicek?

1046
01:42:41,755 --> 01:42:44,975
How quickly you forgot what your
mother did, my daughter

1047
01:42:47,825 --> 01:42:49,855
Don't you guys have brains, Aktemur?

1048
01:42:54,625 --> 01:42:56,325
Ladies!

1049
01:42:57,895 --> 01:43:01,615
This is my tribe, watch your words
and don't raise your voice!

1050
01:43:04,775 --> 01:43:08,805
My husband is a martyr, which game
are you talking about?

1051
01:43:11,305 --> 01:43:14,155
Beys are in a hurry to hold
the inauguration ceremony.

1052
01:43:14,205 --> 01:43:17,975
And I have nothing to hide from Osman Bey.

1053
01:43:17,995 --> 01:43:21,565
We're not going to ask you when we want to
raise our voices, Bengi Hatun.

1054
01:43:21,725 --> 01:43:24,645
It's all been a game of yours,
how can this be free of it?

1055
01:43:25,045 --> 01:43:27,125
You both insisted there was a game

1056
01:43:28,085 --> 01:43:32,555
What game is this? I make my son-in-law
the master of my tribe

1057
01:43:33,515 --> 01:43:38,875
Do you distrust me or Aktemur?

1058
01:43:45,165 --> 01:43:47,995
Aktemur will do exactly what is
required of him

1059
01:43:48,355 --> 01:43:50,205
I trust him fully.

1060
01:43:51,385 --> 01:43:54,365
But I am not satisfied with
this matter, my daughter.

1061
01:43:56,885 --> 01:43:59,175
And this is my final word to you, Aktemur.

1062
01:44:04,185 --> 01:44:07,475
Aktemur, we trust you more
than anyone else.

1063
01:44:08,205 --> 01:44:11,735
But we are not satisfied with this.

1064
01:44:19,495 --> 01:44:21,015
Beys.

1065
01:44:21,645 --> 01:44:23,415
Go to the tent.

1066
01:44:24,285 --> 01:44:25,815
I'm coming.

1067
01:44:41,565 --> 01:44:43,085
The meeting will begin.

1068
01:44:43,695 --> 01:44:45,755
Make up your mind, Aktemur.

1069
01:44:47,575 --> 01:44:49,655
If you say you will receive the trust...

1070
01:44:51,105 --> 01:44:52,655
the meeting is here.

1071
01:44:53,645 --> 01:44:55,515
If you refuse it...

1072
01:44:56,825 --> 01:44:58,685
the door is in that direction.

1073
01:45:08,885 --> 01:45:10,215
Come on.

1074
01:45:10,705 --> 01:45:12,565
Let's not leave the beys waiting.

1075
01:45:18,315 --> 01:45:20,475
Alcicek, come on, my daughter.

1076
01:45:42,245 --> 01:45:43,845
Mother.

1077
01:45:46,775 --> 01:45:48,315
My uncle's wife.

1078
01:45:51,485 --> 01:45:54,025
Why do you object so much to this?

1079
01:45:57,185 --> 01:45:58,755
Aktemur.

1080
01:45:59,285 --> 01:46:01,165
I am not satisfied with this.

1081
01:46:02,345 --> 01:46:04,845
You will not sit on that position.

1082
01:46:09,825 --> 01:46:11,695
Your mother's right, Aktemur.

1083
01:46:12,815 --> 01:46:15,355
Trusting Bengii and sitting
in that position...

1084
01:46:16,585 --> 01:46:18,465
You will only harm yourself.

1085
01:46:53,785 --> 01:46:56,525
Osman, he should have been here.

1086
01:46:56,785 --> 01:46:58,655
Did he understand that it was a trap?

1087
01:47:28,055 --> 01:47:29,585
Osman!

1088
01:47:31,725 --> 01:47:34,455
Send soldiers
to all directions!

1089
01:47:35,595 --> 01:47:37,705
No one will come back until
you find Osman!

1090
01:47:38,945 --> 01:47:43,115
If you don't find Osman,
I will take your souls

1091
01:47:45,375 --> 01:47:48,315
You thought you were a wolf,
and you thought we were sheep

1092
01:47:48,315 --> 01:47:51,005
War in my homeland is not a game.

1093
01:47:51,285 --> 01:47:53,865
Claws are not enough to be a wolf,
you need brains.

1094
01:47:54,145 --> 01:47:56,935
You are missing both, and your
end is near.

1095
01:47:57,385 --> 01:47:58,925
This letter...

1096
01:48:00,375 --> 01:48:03,585
It's your death sentence, Osman.

1097
01:48:04,985 --> 01:48:07,305
Even if I hid well...

1098
01:48:07,965 --> 01:48:10,495
Even if you go down seven
layers underground...

1099
01:48:11,265 --> 01:48:13,145
You will not be able to escape from me.

1100
01:48:16,885 --> 01:48:20,435
I will destroy Yenişehir
over Osman's head.

1101
01:48:21,115 --> 01:48:24,115
Get ready, come on!

1102
01:48:26,145 --> 01:48:29,535
Osman wants to lure you
into a trap, Commander Nayman!

1103
01:48:31,505 --> 01:48:35,095
Trap? What trap can stand before me?

1104
01:48:36,045 --> 01:48:40,905
I am the lion who pulled the arrows
out of his body with his teeth.

1105
01:48:41,765 --> 01:48:43,845
I will destroy Yenişehir.

1106
01:48:44,915 --> 01:48:50,835
Swords will not be sheathed until
none of Osman's descendants remain.

1107
01:48:51,405 --> 01:48:52,725
Come on!

1108
01:48:57,125 --> 01:48:58,445
Sit down.

1109
01:49:04,505 --> 01:49:05,865
Boran.

1110
01:49:06,315 --> 01:49:08,015
What's the situation?

1111
01:49:08,105 --> 01:49:10,125
We've evacuated all the houses, my bey.

1112
01:49:10,235 --> 01:49:12,795
And we've transported the
people safely to Ingol.

1113
01:49:13,455 --> 01:49:16,035
And all the brave ones
whose hands carry arms with us.

1114
01:49:16,915 --> 01:49:19,705
We put gunpowder on every street, my bey.

1115
01:49:20,255 --> 01:49:23,105
They are ready to tear
the infidels to shreds.

1116
01:49:23,735 --> 01:49:25,575
Thank you. Thank you.

1117
01:49:26,605 --> 01:49:29,195
Will you permit me to enter, my bey?

1118
01:49:29,665 --> 01:49:31,175
Come on, Konur.

1119
01:49:38,045 --> 01:49:40,345
Sir, as per your orders,
I was with Bayindir.

1120
01:49:40,675 --> 01:49:43,035
I gave the job to Turgut to come here.

1121
01:49:43,565 --> 01:49:45,845
Thank you. Come.

1122
01:49:47,985 --> 01:49:49,345
Now.

1123
01:49:49,985 --> 01:49:51,985
Turgut and the heroes with him...

1124
01:49:52,475 --> 01:49:54,625
They'll use Bayindir and take the seal.

1125
01:49:56,285 --> 01:49:58,365
And the Sultana Mother and Bala Hatun...

1126
01:49:58,985 --> 01:50:01,815
will go to Konya and destroy Saveli.

1127
01:50:06,185 --> 01:50:07,705
And we...

1128
01:50:09,295 --> 01:50:11,115
...will take care of Nayman's army.

1129
01:50:14,765 --> 01:50:16,575
Will he come, my Bey?

1130
01:50:17,025 --> 01:50:19,635
If he does not come after
my words...

1131
01:50:19,665 --> 01:50:22,295
It means that he is smart enough to
defeat his anger.

1132
01:50:23,075 --> 01:50:25,415
But people like Nayman
rely on their own strength.

1133
01:50:26,255 --> 01:50:29,585
His anger and arrogance
will inevitably overcome him.

1134
01:50:31,255 --> 01:50:32,835
So he will come.

1135
01:50:35,255 --> 01:50:38,105
Now, gather here.

1136
01:50:42,085 --> 01:50:43,435
Come on.

1137
01:50:45,165 --> 01:50:46,795
Most importantly...

1138
01:50:47,865 --> 01:50:50,435
Their first target will be our mansion.

1139
01:50:51,555 --> 01:50:55,135
For this reason,
you will place archers on rooftops.

1140
01:50:56,155 --> 01:50:57,695
in these places...

1141
01:50:59,535 --> 01:51:01,045
Then...

1142
01:51:01,635 --> 01:51:03,025
My sons...

1143
01:51:03,765 --> 01:51:05,625
Come closer and listen to me well.

1144
01:51:10,265 --> 01:51:12,425
Aladdin, Orhan

1145
01:51:13,685 --> 01:51:15,775
Soldiers who will try to enter from here...

1146
01:51:16,185 --> 01:51:18,345
You will drive them back with your arrows.

1147
01:51:19,615 --> 01:51:22,115
Do you understand, sons?

1148
01:51:22,485 --> 01:51:24,065
Your command, my Bey.

1149
01:51:24,065 --> 01:51:25,325
Thank you.

1150
01:51:25,345 --> 01:51:26,665
The command is yours, my Bey.

1151
01:51:26,755 --> 01:51:28,125
Thank you.

1152
01:51:29,235 --> 01:51:31,015
And for us...

1153
01:51:32,095 --> 01:51:34,125
The rest of the Mongol soldiers
will be in the field.

1154
01:51:36,035 --> 01:51:40,095
We will drag them to the places where
we have previously put the gunpowder.

1155
01:51:43,645 --> 01:51:45,805
When the soldiers are pushed back...

1156
01:51:46,105 --> 01:51:47,965
Baysungur, Aykurt.

1157
01:51:48,385 --> 01:51:50,675
You will light the gunpowder on both sides.

1158
01:51:51,935 --> 01:51:53,935
Even if they run away from the fire...

1159
01:51:54,035 --> 01:51:56,235
They will not be able to
escape from the boiling oils

1160
01:51:56,465 --> 01:51:58,015
Okay, my Bey.

1161
01:51:58,055 --> 01:52:00,475
Let's see how high
the Mongol soldiers can fly.

1162
01:52:01,015 --> 01:52:03,325
Mongol soldiers are like birds, my Bey.

1163
01:52:05,165 --> 01:52:07,625
Yes, yes.

1164
01:52:08,735 --> 01:52:12,615
He who harbors anger accompanies death.

1165
01:52:14,795 --> 01:52:16,105
Come to me, Nayman.

1166
01:52:57,585 --> 01:53:00,095
Nobody's coming,
who are we waiting for, Bengi Hatun?

1167
01:53:00,505 --> 01:53:02,475
Where is the Bey you said you'd bring?

1168
01:53:04,985 --> 01:53:06,845
I don't think Bey is coming.

1169
01:53:06,935 --> 01:53:08,765
So, we will choose our own Bey.

1170
01:53:09,055 --> 01:53:10,565
Right, Beys?

1171
01:53:10,575 --> 01:53:12,165
- Yes, we can.
- That's right.

1172
01:53:12,235 --> 01:53:13,045
He is right.

1173
01:53:13,045 --> 01:53:14,045
Mother.

1174
01:53:15,525 --> 01:53:17,055
He won't come.

1175
01:53:20,285 --> 01:53:22,095
He made a choice.

1176
01:53:23,495 --> 01:53:25,705
We will take care of ourselves.

1177
01:53:31,265 --> 01:53:33,855
This is not the time to stand idly,
we have to choose

1178
01:53:36,455 --> 01:53:37,995
Beys!

1179
01:54:01,385 --> 01:54:03,395
As the new Bey of the Kargin tribe...

1180
01:54:04,745 --> 01:54:06,285
I nominate my son-in-law

1181
01:54:07,615 --> 01:54:10,175
Aktemur, Gunduz Bey's son.

1182
01:54:17,825 --> 01:54:19,825
If anyone objects...

1183
01:54:23,045 --> 01:54:24,635
Speak now.

1184
01:54:24,685 --> 01:54:27,055
You recommend Aktemur in order to...

1185
01:54:27,065 --> 01:54:29,155
...keep us captive under Kayis!

1186
01:54:40,075 --> 01:54:41,895
What captivity are you talking about?

1187
01:54:43,915 --> 01:54:46,995
Hasn't Kayi been fighting for
generations for your freedom?

1188
01:54:47,805 --> 01:54:50,825
What do you accuse of those who offer their blood
so that you do not fall into captivity!

1189
01:54:50,855 --> 01:54:52,935
It's not an accusation, it's the truth

1190
01:54:53,215 --> 01:54:55,235
Do you know what the truth is?

1191
01:54:57,405 --> 01:54:59,435
You no longer have a place in this meeting.

1192
01:54:59,515 --> 01:55:01,535
Who are you to kick me out of here?

1193
01:55:01,605 --> 01:55:03,735
I am the Bey of Kargin tribe!

1194
01:55:06,005 --> 01:55:07,525
Get lost!

1195
01:55:25,985 --> 01:55:28,525
Bless your Beyship, Aktemur Bey.

1196
01:55:28,775 --> 01:55:30,145
So...

1197
01:55:37,925 --> 01:55:39,925
Bless your Beyship, Aktemur Bey.

1198
01:56:11,655 --> 01:56:12,975
Now...

1199
01:56:14,275 --> 01:56:17,195
The sword is yours, the throne is yours.

1200
01:56:21,755 --> 01:56:23,485
And the Kargin tribe is yours.

1201
01:56:30,935 --> 01:56:32,255
Kutlu!

1202
01:57:37,025 --> 01:57:39,885
I hand over the trust to its owner.

1203
01:57:40,975 --> 01:57:42,335
Do you witness, Beys?

1204
01:57:42,385 --> 01:57:43,605
Yes.

1205
01:57:43,625 --> 01:57:44,755
Do you witness, Beys?

1206
01:57:44,815 --> 01:57:45,935
Yes.

1207
01:57:45,945 --> 01:57:47,955
- Do you witness, Beys?
- Yes!

1208
01:58:00,425 --> 01:58:02,225
Your entrust is my entrust.

1209
01:58:05,725 --> 01:58:07,555
And your children are my children.

1210
01:58:12,675 --> 01:58:14,555
And your soul is my soul.

1211
01:58:24,915 --> 01:58:26,785
Now that you trust me...

1212
01:58:27,305 --> 01:58:29,365
And you accepted me as your Bey...

1213
01:58:30,455 --> 01:58:32,275
I will sacrifice my life on your way.

1214
01:58:34,525 --> 01:58:36,035
Shall be blessed.

1215
01:58:36,115 --> 01:58:37,685
Shall be blessed.

1216
01:59:55,485 --> 01:59:57,075
Let's see.

1217
02:00:57,665 --> 02:00:59,205
O Allah

1218
02:01:08,305 --> 02:01:09,855
O Right!

1219
02:01:18,735 --> 02:01:20,295
O Right!

1220
02:01:28,285 --> 02:01:30,345
Allah is the greatest!

1221
02:01:32,305 --> 02:01:33,835
Come to me.

1222
02:01:41,325 --> 02:01:42,825
O Right!

1223
02:01:48,605 --> 02:01:50,495
Come on, you dogs!

1224
02:01:59,265 --> 02:02:00,965
Split up!

1225
02:02:08,605 --> 02:02:10,175
You dogs.

1226
02:02:10,625 --> 02:02:12,195
O Allah!

1227
02:02:57,615 --> 02:02:59,675
Oh Right!

1228
02:03:29,885 --> 02:03:31,395
Alps!

1229
02:03:39,435 --> 02:03:41,505
Getting out of Yenişehir is not that simple

1230
02:03:41,565 --> 02:03:44,075
Come on, O Allah!

1231
02:06:25,555 --> 02:06:31,725
Allah is the greatest!

1232
02:06:31,775 --> 02:06:34,795
Allah is the greatest!

1233
02:06:37,915 --> 02:06:42,995
Sir, we killed a few of them
but there are many waiting for us outside

1234
02:06:53,705 --> 02:06:55,765
How long is left for iftar, Hussein?

1235
02:06:56,765 --> 02:06:58,635
It's still early, my Bey.

1236
02:06:58,665 --> 02:07:00,215
We got hungry!

1237
02:07:00,525 --> 02:07:02,535
Yes my Bey, we got hungry.

1238
02:07:03,035 --> 02:07:05,575
Let's take that seal, Hussein.

1239
02:07:05,995 --> 02:07:10,025
And then our age will begin, I hope so.

1240
02:07:10,715 --> 02:07:14,265
It will begin, my Bey, it will begin.

1241
02:07:19,605 --> 02:07:21,395
It's a trap, alps!

1242
02:07:34,945 --> 02:07:37,525
Where is Bayindir going like this?

1243
02:07:39,765 --> 02:07:43,095
And I was wondering if
the infidels were the ones blocking our way!

1244
02:07:46,015 --> 02:07:50,105
What's it, Turgut Bey?
Have you come to spill the blood of your brothers?

1245
02:07:50,175 --> 02:07:54,435
Not at all, not the blood of the brother,
but I will spill the blood of the ignoble!

1246
02:07:57,115 --> 02:07:58,975
Haven't you seen this coming?

1247
02:08:00,355 --> 02:08:03,495
Did you think we wouldn't hold you
accountable after all the betrayal?

1248
02:08:07,045 --> 02:08:10,645
Get out of my way and
I will forgive you for what you said.

1249
02:08:14,565 --> 02:08:18,245
No need to do that.
You're exposed.

1250
02:08:18,535 --> 02:08:22,035
You work with
Nayman, and everyone knows it.

1251
02:08:25,255 --> 02:08:29,325
This means that Osman
was not deceived by all this.

1252
02:08:29,585 --> 02:08:30,955
Yes.

1253
02:08:36,885 --> 02:08:39,095
Know that I will not give up.

1254
02:08:39,335 --> 02:08:42,755
That's not going to help
you, Bayındır, what are you going to do?

1255
02:08:48,915 --> 02:08:52,225
I will say for once, you have
no way out of here.

1256
02:08:53,235 --> 02:08:56,735
You are all prisoners and your
convoy is our property.

1257
02:09:00,135 --> 02:09:02,195
It's not that easy, Turgut.

1258
02:09:03,135 --> 02:09:04,505
Come here.

1259
02:09:25,265 --> 02:09:29,665
I bear witness that there is no
deity but Allah...

1260
02:09:29,675 --> 02:09:33,735
and I bear witness that Muhammad
is His servant and Messenger.

1261
02:09:34,705 --> 02:09:37,545
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

1262
02:09:48,865 --> 02:09:52,675
Not yet.
We need you.

1263
02:09:56,575 --> 02:09:57,915
Stand up.

1264
02:09:59,555 --> 02:10:04,335
But you're going to do something you
know this time, you're going to betray Nayman.

1265
02:10:06,055 --> 02:10:09,215
And then you'll give us that very
valuable seal.

1266
02:10:11,505 --> 02:10:14,495
Kutan, tie him to the back of the cart.

1267
02:10:15,975 --> 02:10:17,295
Your command, my Bey.

1268
02:10:20,015 --> 02:10:21,315
Come on.

1269
02:10:28,605 --> 02:10:31,365
Konya Palace

1270
02:10:35,850 --> 02:10:38,570
Celali, find Vizier Saveli.

1271
02:10:42,620 --> 02:10:44,800
We will find my son, Bala Hatun.

1272
02:10:45,240 --> 02:10:46,800
Come on then.

1273
02:10:51,340 --> 02:10:53,090
Mother Sultan.

1274
02:10:56,160 --> 02:10:58,220
Vizier Saveli knows we're coming.

1275
02:10:58,300 --> 02:11:01,550
Let's split our forces to find Sultan
Aladdin as soon as possible.

1276
02:11:02,570 --> 02:11:04,400
This is very dangerous, Bala Hatun.

1277
02:11:04,600 --> 02:11:06,600
We have no other solution, Mother Sultan.

1278
02:11:06,810 --> 02:11:10,080
The only power that will stop Saveli
is the power of Sultan Aladdin.

1279
02:11:13,320 --> 02:11:14,870
Be careful.

1280
02:11:15,420 --> 02:11:16,740
Okay.

1281
02:11:16,890 --> 02:11:18,680
May our conquest be blessed.

1282
02:11:41,710 --> 02:11:43,260
Alps!

1283
02:11:45,820 --> 02:11:47,330
Sisters.

1284
02:11:59,950 --> 02:12:01,490
Bala Hatun.

1285
02:12:10,200 --> 02:12:13,000
To whom is the intention and
to whom is the share?

1286
02:12:13,420 --> 02:12:15,300
I was waiting for Mother Sultan.

1287
02:12:17,360 --> 02:12:19,210
Don't worry, Saveli.

1288
02:12:19,250 --> 02:12:21,790
Either she kills you or I do.

1289
02:12:24,830 --> 02:12:26,640
Where is the Sultan Aladdin?

1290
02:12:27,210 --> 02:12:29,760
- If he's hurt...
- He is.

1291
02:12:32,110 --> 02:12:35,880
I'll give his head as a gift to Nayman.

1292
02:12:36,140 --> 02:12:39,340
But you won't even see it.

1293
02:12:42,110 --> 02:12:45,620
When the lion enters the trap,
then even the foxes become strong.

1294
02:12:45,920 --> 02:12:49,960
Move to cut off your heads.

1295
02:12:53,690 --> 02:12:55,520
Time has passed.

1296
02:12:56,760 --> 02:13:00,260
I am the lion and I am the wolf.

1297
02:13:27,600 --> 02:13:28,920
Attack!

1298
02:13:30,382 --> 02:13:35,262
Everybody, get ready! We'll get
in when we get the news.

1299
02:13:40,605 --> 02:13:42,925
There are horsemen
coming, Commander Nayman.

1300
02:13:43,355 --> 02:13:45,195
Soldiers, get ready.

1301
02:13:45,465 --> 02:13:50,045
Blood, blood, blood!

1302
02:13:50,135 --> 02:14:02,645
Blood, blood, blood!

1303
02:14:23,695 --> 02:14:25,235
Nayman.

1304
02:14:26,985 --> 02:14:29,015
Are you hiding behind your soldiers?

1305
02:14:29,465 --> 02:14:31,465
Why don't you appear in front of me?

1306
02:14:33,495 --> 02:14:35,375
You defended your city...

1307
02:14:35,945 --> 02:14:37,495
and you killed my soldiers.

1308
02:14:38,325 --> 02:14:39,845
You must be tired.

1309
02:14:40,445 --> 02:14:42,255
But what about me?

1310
02:14:43,195 --> 02:14:46,235
I'm just angry.

1311
02:14:47,065 --> 02:14:49,595
I will kill you.

1312
02:14:51,005 --> 02:14:53,535
And I have my faith.

1313
02:14:54,975 --> 02:14:58,025
Will this protect you from my wrath?

1314
02:14:58,665 --> 02:15:01,165
Your anger will be your end.

1315
02:15:04,045 --> 02:15:07,435
I will show you the
last drop of my mercy.

1316
02:15:10,185 --> 02:15:12,215
We will not shed blood anymore.

1317
02:15:13,095 --> 02:15:14,915
It's the last blood, Osman.

1318
02:15:15,835 --> 02:15:17,175
Say it.

1319
02:15:17,935 --> 02:15:23,025
Tomorrow at sunset, you will come
to the site of the Karaoluk.

1320
02:15:23,435 --> 02:15:25,995
You and I only.

1321
02:15:26,655 --> 02:15:28,415
We'll go out to the arena.

1322
02:15:29,385 --> 02:15:34,095
Only one of us will make it out alive.

1323
02:15:34,905 --> 02:15:36,445
Last blood, Osman.

1324
02:15:38,615 --> 02:15:39,895
Okay.

1325
02:15:40,495 --> 02:15:46,695
When I show up at the arena, it
will be mine when I draw my sword.

1326
02:15:47,805 --> 02:15:49,375
I accept that.

1327
02:15:51,485 --> 02:15:56,035
Your soldiers will leave my
lands when I kill you.

1328
02:15:59,185 --> 02:16:00,975
Tell your Beys.

1329
02:16:03,105 --> 02:16:07,655
You will obey!

1330
02:16:09,005 --> 02:16:14,085
When I kill you, you won't even
have a grave in those lands.

1331
02:16:26,815 --> 02:16:58,205
Visit our website for more: turkision.com